'byline': {'original': 'By Paul Krugman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Paul', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Krugman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/6dc7b2b5-f7d8-50bc-b829-54ff3e8a2423', 'word_count': 945, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6dc7b2b5-f7d8-50bc-b829-54ff3e8a2423'}, {'abstract': 'Sam Ezersky gets a little feisty, and a little zeitgeisty.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2019/05/04/crosswords/variety-puns-and-anagrams.html', 'snippet': 'Sam Ezersky gets a little feisty, and a little zeitgeisty.', 'lead_paragraph': 'VARIETY PUZZLE  — Puns are inventive and complex; whenever you think you’ve pinned down every type of pun under the sun, something new (at least to you) inevitably pops up.  Anagrams, on the other hand, are pretty linear, the multiple choice questions of puzzling. The letters you need to fill in your entry are right in front of you — you just need to figure out which ones, then scramble them up to make some sense.  ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Variety: Puns and Anagrams', 'kicker': 'SUNDAY VARIETY COLUMN', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Crossword Puzzles', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Ezersky, Sam', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2019-05-04T15:40:01+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Games', 'section_name': 'Crosswords & Games', 'byline': {'original': 'By Caitlin Lovinger', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Caitlin', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Lovinger', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/8aeeb0f4-bed9-5c23-8829-010250fbad6c', 'word_count': 617, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8aeeb0f4-bed9-5c23-8829-010250fbad6c'}, {'abstract': 'During trade talks, U.S. officials have avoided confronting China about its persecution of Uighurs despite bipartisan pressure, fearing such a move could harm a deal.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2019/05/04/world/asia/trump-china-uighurs-trade-deal.html', 'snippet': 'During trade talks, U.S. officials have avoided confronting China about its persecution of Uighurs despite bipartisan pressure, fearing such a move could harm a deal.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WASHINGTON — The United States and China are racing to clinch a historic economic treaty as early as next week that could drastically reshape relations between the world’s two largest economies. But as negotiations reach their final stages, the sensitive subject of human rights has been left conspicuously off the table.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '12', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/05/05/business/05-DC-UIGHRS-p1/merlin_154339449_b5f18e6e-b751-46a1-a217-e49b5311979b-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2019/05/05/business/05-DC-UIGHRS-p1/merlin_154339449_b5f18e6e-b751-46a1-a217-e49b5311979b-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/05/05/business/05-DC-UIGHRS-p1/merlin_154339449_b5f18e6e-b751-46a1-a217-e49b5311979b-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/05/05/business/05-DC-UIGHRS-p1/merlin_154339449_b5f18e6e-b751-46a1-a217-e49b5311979b-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None