Clifford Krauss', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Clifford', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Krauss', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/8a3a0afb-b6ff-5a0e-bfb6-f3107311cccb', 'word_count': 679, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8a3a0afb-b6ff-5a0e-bfb6-f3107311cccb'}, {'abstract': 'Kanter, the outspoken N.B.A. star, will be fasting for Ramadan as usual this year, but, in a first, he will be competing in the playoffs at the same time.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2019/05/05/sports/enes-kanter-ramadan-fasting.html', 'snippet': 'Kanter, the outspoken N.B.A. star, will be fasting for Ramadan as usual this year, but, in a first, he will be competing in the playoffs at the same time.', 'lead_paragraph': 'On Monday, around 4 a.m., Enes Kanter will wake up, eat a light breakfast of yogurt, fruit and peanut butter, and drink as much water as he can. Then for the roughly 16 hours between sunrise and sunset in Portland, Ore., the center for the Portland Trail Blazers will abstain from eating, drinking and taking medicine, even for the shoulder he separated almost two weeks ago. For Kanter, a Swiss-born Turk who has fasted for Ramadan while playing competitive basketball for the past decade, the routine is nothing new. But this time, the circumstances may be: Never before has he fasted while playing in the N.B.A.’s postseason.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/05/06/sports/06Kanter-illo/merlin_154428891_9b3163bb-4889-49cd-9e1c-3e966c7aedb8-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 644, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2019/05/06/sports/06Kanter-illo/merlin_154428891_9b3163bb-4889-49cd-9e1c-3e966c7aedb8-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 644}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/05/06/sports/06Kanter-illo/merlin_154428891_9b3163bb-4889-49cd-9e1c-3e966c7aedb8-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 955, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/05/06/sports/06Kanter-illo/merlin_154428891_9b3163bb-4889-49cd-9e1c-3e966c7aedb8-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1909, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/05/06/sports/06Kanter-illo/06Kanter-illo-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2019/05/06/sports/06Kanter-illo/06Kanter-illo-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/05/06/sports/06Kanter-illo/06Kanter-illo-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'While Enes Kanter is Observing Ramadan, the World Will Be Watching Him', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Pregame Meal: 4 A.M.', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Basketball', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Playoff Games', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Ramadan', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Fasting', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Muslims and Islam', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Portland Trail Blazers', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Kanter, Enes', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2019-05-05T22:30:07+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'byline': {'original': 'By Spenser Mestel', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Spenser', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Mestel', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b488dbe8-4fe9-570c-9e34-b2928608dcc6', 'word_count': 1140, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b488dbe8-4fe9-570c-9e34-b2928608dcc6'}, {'abstract': 'Why else would he pursue so many policies in Latin America that do not serve the national interest?', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2019/05/05/opinion/trump-venezuela-cuba.html', 'snippet': 'Why else would he pursue so many policies in Latin America that do not serve the national interest?', 'lead_paragraph': 'Americans can be forgiven if they struggle to find any coherence in the Trump administration’s foreign policy. It zigs and zags, with senior administration officials saying one thing and President Trump contradicting them without warning the next day. It punishes our allies and coddles our adversaries; it privileges demagogy over democracy. Mr. Trump’s approach appears impulsive, improvisational and inchoate — devoid of clear purpose, values or even ideology.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '23', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/05/05/opinion/05rice/05rice-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 600, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2019/05/05/opinion/05rice/05rice-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 600}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/05/05/opinion/05rice/05rice-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'supe