onight!', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2019/05/06/dining/watermelon-trifle-recipes.html', 'snippet': 'Tejal Rao has a new recipe for a watermelon-rose trifle inspired by one she had in Australia. Make it tonight!', 'lead_paragraph': 'Good morning. Tejal Rao has a lovely column in The Times this week about a cake that’s famous on Instagram, that she ate one time in Australia and that she spent three years thinking about how to make at home before coming to the conclusion that the best thing to do was to not even try, but to prepare the basic components and cobble them together into a watermelon-rose trifle (above) to deliver all the flavors with none of the exacting work.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/05/05/magazine/05mag-eat-slideshow-slide-NHZH-copy/05mag-eat-slideshow-slide-NHZH-articleLarge.png', 'height': 450, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2019/05/05/magazine/05mag-eat-slideshow-slide-NHZH-copy/05mag-eat-slideshow-slide-NHZH-articleLarge.png', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 450}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/05/05/magazine/05mag-eat-slideshow-slide-NHZH-copy/05mag-eat-slideshow-slide-NHZH-jumbo.png', 'height': 768, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/05/05/magazine/05mag-eat-slideshow-slide-NHZH-copy/05mag-eat-slideshow-slide-NHZH-superJumbo.png', 'height': 1536, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/05/05/magazine/05mag-eat-slideshow-slide-NHZH-copy/05mag-eat-slideshow-slide-NHZH-thumbStandard.png', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2019/05/05/magazine/05mag-eat-slideshow-slide-NHZH-copy/05mag-eat-slideshow-slide-NHZH-thumbStandard.png', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/05/05/magazine/05mag-eat-slideshow-slide-NHZH-copy/05mag-eat-slideshow-slide-NHZH-thumbLarge.png', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'What to Cook Right Now', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cooking and Cookbooks', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2019-05-06T14:30:01+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Dining', 'section_name': 'Food', 'byline': {'original': 'By Sam Sifton', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Sam', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Sifton', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/783b9162-0e79-567a-89d8-1a7ab804c0e3', 'word_count': 465, 'uri': 'nyt://article/783b9162-0e79-567a-89d8-1a7ab804c0e3'}, {'abstract': 'We have a right to practice our beliefs, but we don’t have the right to discriminate against others, or endanger their lives.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2019/05/06/opinion/vaccines-religious-freedom.html', 'snippet': 'We have a right to practice our beliefs, but we don’t have the right to discriminate against others, or endanger their lives.', 'lead_paragraph': 'NASHVILLE — In 1976 I left a small Catholic grammar school, where we prayed aloud four times a day, to attend a large public high school where we didn’t pray aloud at all. The United States Supreme Court had banned school-sponsored prayer in 1962, but nobody was keeping me from praying. I prayed for help on my biology test. I prayed for the red-haired boy in Alabama History to smile at me, and I gave a little prayer of thanksgiving when he did. I offered up silent prayers of astonishment and silent prayers of gratitude and silent prayers for peace — peace for my own agitated heart and peace for the whole agitated world. I prayed all day long, and no one in my public school had any idea I was praying at all.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/05/06/opinion/06renklWeb/merlin_153287679_c47dc945-2a25-436f-9dfe-9a6964ca31f3-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 399, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2019/05/06/opinion/06renklWeb/merlin_153287679_c47dc945-2a25-436f-9dfe-9a6964ca31f3-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 399}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/05/06/opinion/06renklWeb/merlin_153287679_c47dc945-2a25-436f-9dfe-9a6964ca31f3-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 680, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/05/06/opinion/06renklWeb/merlin_153287679_c47dc945-2a25-436f-9dfe-9a6964ca31f3-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1360, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/05/06/opinion/06renklWeb/06renklWeb-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2019/05/06/opinion/06renklWeb/06renklWeb-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/05/