et.html', 'snippet': 'An occasional cabaret in the upstairs lounge called the Treehouse stars current and former employees.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The plush blue lounge upstairs at the Four Seasons Restaurant has started holding cabaret performances on occasional Friday evenings. What is uncommon about the programs is that many of the performers are current or former kitchen and dining room employees of the restaurant. In April, Rafa Campos Salles, a former reservationist, performed Poulenc and a medley of Broadway oldies, accompanied by Monica Lu, and they may return on May 31. Nick Drakides, a former bartender, will perform jazz on May 17. In July, Carson Rammelt, a singer, songwriter and Four Seasons host, will be onstage at a date yet to be determined. A bar menu, with oysters, Wagyu sliders, crab cakes and arancini, is available.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/06/06/dining/06burner6/06burner6-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2019/06/06/dining/06burner6/06burner6-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/06/06/dining/06burner6/06burner6-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/06/06/dining/06burner6/06burner6-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/06/06/dining/06burner6/06burner6-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2019/06/06/dining/06burner6/06burner6-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/06/06/dining/06burner6/06burner6-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'The Staff Sings at the Four Seasons', 'kicker': 'Front Burner', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'To Entertain: The Staff Sings At the Four Seasons', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Restaurants', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Four Seasons Restaurant (Manhattan, NY)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2019-05-07T02:20:01+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Dining', 'section_name': 'Food', 'byline': {'original': 'By Florence Fabricant', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Florence', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Fabricant', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/034eb741-726b-5f07-83b6-8cb1a154c6d6', 'word_count': 164, 'uri': 'nyt://article/034eb741-726b-5f07-83b6-8cb1a154c6d6'}, {'abstract': 'Tama Matsuoka Wong, the forager for Restaurant Daniel, has released a new bottled tea, made with sumac.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2019/05/06/dining/drinks/i-am-a-weed-sumac-tea.html', 'snippet': 'Tama Matsuoka Wong, the forager for Restaurant Daniel, has released a new bottled tea, made with sumac.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The bold capital letters on the tea label say “weed,” but it’s not the smokable kind. Tama Matsuoka Wong — the forager par excellence, who works with Restaurant Daniel and has written a book about foraging — has introduced bottled sumac tea, her first product in the I Am a Weed line from Tama’s Wild Teas. The deep red pointed berry clusters of sumac, a plant native to the northeastern United States (and the Middle East), were used to make a beverage by the inhabitants of the region long before European settlers arrived. I Am a Weed Sumac Tea is light brown, refreshingly tart and judiciously sweetened with agave.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/05/08/dining/06burner4/06burner4-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2019/05/08/dining/06burner4/06burner4-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/05/08/dining/06burner4/06burner4-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 682, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/05/08/dining/06burner4/06burner4-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/05/08/dining/06burner4/06burner4-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2019/05/08/dining/06burner4/06burner4-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/05/08/dining/06burner4/06burner4-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'The Forager Steeps a Tea', 'kicker': 'Front Burner', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'To Refresh: The Forager  Steeps a Tea', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Tea', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Weeds', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Wong, Tama Matsuoka', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': "Tama's Wild Teas", 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2019-05-07T02:21:58+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Dining', 'section_name': 'Food', 'subsection_name': 'Wine, Beer & Cocktails', 'byline': {'original': 'By Florence Fabricant', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Florence', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Fabricant', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d3a5e6d2-9ec0-5679-b42b-3be93406c746', 'word_count': 146, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d3a5e6d2-9ec0-5679-b42b-3be93406c746'}, {'abstract': 'Florentine knives were born in Israel and honed in Barcelona. They’re now available online.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2019/05/06/dining/florentine-knives.html', 'snippet': 'Florentine knives were born in Israel and honed in Barcelona. They’re now available online.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Tomer Botner, an industrial designer, started making Florentine kitchen knives in his apartment in Tel Aviv, in the Florentin neighborhood. He kept the name of the company after relocating to Barcelona with his wife, Noam Blumenthal, and his stunning knives are now available online. Each knife he sells is custom-made from a choice of blades (French carbon steel or Swedish high carbon stainless steel) and handles (striped micarta — a composite of various materials sealed in a plastic resin — and wood). There are three models: a paring knife with a 4-inch blade; a dramatically curved and beautifully balanced chef’s knife, with an 8-inch blade, and a steak knife. Mr. Botner has a few in stock, ready to ship. Custom orders take 10 weeks.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/05/08/dining/06burner2/06burner2-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 347, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2019/05/08/dining/06burner2/06burner2-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 347}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/05/08/dining/06burner2/06burner2-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 593, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/05/08/dining/06burner2/06burner2-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1186, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/05/08/dining/06burner2/06burner2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2019/05/08/dining/06burner2/06burner2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/05/08/dining/06burner2/06burner2-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'A Knife Made for You', 'kicker': 'Front Burner', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'To Slice: A Florentine Knife  Made for You', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Knives', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Botner, Tomer', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Florentine Kitchen Knives', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Barcelona (Spain)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2019-05-07T02:24:04+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Dining', 'section_name': 'Food', 'byline': {'original': 'By Florence Fabricant', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Florence', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Fabricant', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/49896a22-af6b-55eb-bfde-46994d5fb032', 'word_count': 156, 'uri': 'nyt://article/49896a22-af6b-55eb-bfde-46994d5fb032'}, {'abstract': 'George Perrot served nearly 30 years in prison for a rape conviction after a trial based on flawed evidence. Now he has been charged again in a separate case.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2019/05/06/us/george-perrot-rape-charges.html', 'snippet': 'George Perrot served nearly 30 years in prison for a rape conviction after a trial based on flawed evidence. Now he has been charged again in a separate case.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A Massachusetts man who served nearly 30 years in prison after he was wrongly convicted of rape was arraigned on new rape charges Monday in an unrelated case after the police said he assaulted an unconscious woman on a sidewalk.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '16', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/05/06/multimedia/06xp-rape/merlin_154470099_016bebe0-72e8-48bf-abb2-a347a672c6fd-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 425, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2019/05/06/multimedia/06xp-rape/merlin_154470099_016bebe0-72e8-48bf-abb2-a347a672c6fd-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 425}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/05/06/multimedia/06xp-rape/merlin_154470099_016bebe0-72e8-48bf-abb2-a347a672c6fd-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 725, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/05/06/multimedia/06xp-rape/merlin_154470099_016bebe0-72e8-48bf-abb2-a347a672c6fd-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1449, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/05/06/multimedia/06xp-rape/06xp-rape-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2019/05/06/multimedia/06xp-rape/06xp-rape-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/05/06/multimedia/06xp-rape/06xp-rape-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Man Once Wrongly Convicted of Rape Now Faces Rape Charge in a New Case', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'New Rape Charge for Man Once Wrongly Convicted', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Perrot, George', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Sex Crimes', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'False Arrests, Convictions and Imprisonments', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Lawrence (Mass)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2019-05-07T02:27:45+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Express', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Liam Stack', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Liam', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Stack', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/1d99e882-f330-5617-b6b8-2aaeeb3c05fa', 'word_count': 803, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1d99e882-f330-5617-b6b8-2aaeeb3c05fa'}, {'abstract': '“20 Recipes Kids Should Know” is the work of Esme Washburn, a New York home cook, and her photographer sister, Calista, 17.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2019/05/06/dining/20-recipes-kids-should-know-cookbook.html', 'snippet': '“20 Recipes Kids Should Know” is the work of Esme Washburn, a New York home cook, and her photographer sister, Calista, 17.', 'lead_paragraph': 'From the mouths of preteens? This cookbook for the younger set was written by a 12-year-old, who certainly knows her way around the kitchen and is armed with intelligent vocabulary (a grilled cheese is “quintessential”). The bright photos are the work of her older sister, 17. The recipes, all basic, are not meant to be kid-friendly (though some call for adult supervision), what with black bean soup starting with dried beans, pasta made from scratch and yeast-raised dough for pizza. Some of the text has nice personal touches about cooking with Grandma and the like.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/05/08/dining/06burner1/06burner1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 721, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2019/05/08/dining/06burner1/06burner1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 721}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/05/08/dining/06burner1/06burner1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 852, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/05/08/dining/06burner1/06burner1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1704, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/05/08/dining/06burner1/06burner1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2019/05/08/dining/06burner1/06burner1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/05/08/dining/06burner1/06burner1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'At 12, She’s Written Her First Cookbook', 'kicker': 'Front Burner', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'To Learn: An Early Start For Young Cooks', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cooking and Cookbooks', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Washburn, Esme', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': '20 Recipes Kids Should Know (Book)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2019-05-07T02:28:34+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Dining', 'section_name': 'Food', 'byline': {'original': 'By Florence Fabricant', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Florence', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Fabricant', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/59d0ed90-83c7-51c6-a709-bd68b2f36e8a', 'word_count': 135, 'uri': 'nyt://article/59d0ed90-83c7-51c6-a709-bd68b2f36e8a'}, {'abstract': 'Iberian Pastures sells its heirloom Ibérico pork online.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2019/05/06/dining/american-iberico-pork.html', 'snippet': 'Iberian Pastures sells its heirloom Ibérico pork online.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Iberian Pastures in Bluffton, Ga., has raised heirloom black-hoof Ibérico pigs for about five years. The breed, imported from Spain, has thrived on a diet of peanuts, pecans and sunflower seeds. While the pork — rich and succulent Ibérico for enjoying fresh or cured — has been sold to restaurants, it’s now available retail. Cuts from the loin are magnificently flavorful and tender when grilled or seared on a plancha. Other cuts, like cheeks, are meant for braising. Some Spanish pieces, like secreto and abanico, are described as similar to flank or skirt steak, but I found them thin, uneven and not entirely satisfying. I liked these best cut in strips, marinated and stir-fried. Familiar cuts like tenderloin tend to sell out quickly, though they are replenished regularly.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/06/08/dining/06burner7/merlin_154148262_812e2fe6-918c-429c-99aa-176956f6188b-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2019/06/08/dining/06burner7/merlin_154148262_812e2fe6-918c-429c-99aa-176956f6188b-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/06/08/dining/06burner7/merlin_154148262_812e2fe6-918c-429c-99aa-176956f6188b-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/06/08/dining/06burner7/merlin_154148262_812e2fe6-918c-429c-99aa-176956f6188b-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1367, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit