: [{'firstname': 'Malia', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Wollan', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/4428f026-660b-524b-adbc-011cd301836f', 'word_count': 391, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4428f026-660b-524b-adbc-011cd301836f'}, {'abstract': 'Some 32-inch footprints were found in the mountains of Nepal. Could they belong to the infamous yeti?', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2019/05/07/learning/what-legends-and-myths-do-you-believe-in.html', 'snippet': 'Some 32-inch footprints were found in the mountains of Nepal. Could they belong to the infamous yeti?', 'lead_paragraph': 'Have you ever seen or heard of Bigfoot? An apelike creature about 6 feet 9 inches, covered in black, dark brown or dark reddish hair, who enjoys roaming remote parts of North America? Or so it is said.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/04/30/us/politics/30xp-yeti-01/merlin_154176399_f6bad11d-4aad-4083-b103-161ff7771dcf-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 900, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2019/04/30/us/politics/30xp-yeti-01/merlin_154176399_f6bad11d-4aad-4083-b103-161ff7771dcf-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 900}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/04/30/us/politics/30xp-yeti-01/merlin_154176399_f6bad11d-4aad-4083-b103-161ff7771dcf-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 683, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/04/30/us/politics/30xp-yeti-01/merlin_154176399_f6bad11d-4aad-4083-b103-161ff7771dcf-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1366, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/04/30/us/politics/30xp-yeti-01/30xp-yeti-01-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2019/04/30/us/politics/30xp-yeti-01/30xp-yeti-01-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/04/30/us/politics/30xp-yeti-01/30xp-yeti-01-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'What Legends and Myths Do You Believe In?', 'kicker': 'Student Opinion', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2019-05-07T09:00:03+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Learning', 'section_name': 'The Learning Network', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jeremy Engle', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jeremy', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Engle', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/533064a6-1db7-5974-844a-d422f512b3ba', 'word_count': 767, 'uri': 'nyt://article/533064a6-1db7-5974-844a-d422f512b3ba'}, {'abstract': 'Over a 40-year career, the actress has avoided being typecast and explored humor in broken places.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2019/05/07/magazine/laura-dern-little-women.html', 'snippet': 'Over a 40-year career, the actress has avoided being typecast and explored humor in broken places.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Laura Dern’s face is elastic. It’s superelastic. It can do more stuff than a normal face can. You’ve seen it yourself, how it goes slack jawed and gooey in Steven Spielberg’s “Jurassic Park” or opens screaming like the jaws of hell while she plays three — or is it four? — characters in David Lynch’s epic of psychic disintegration, “Inland Empire.” Or recall the three-minute breakdown that begins the pilot episode of the 2011 HBO series “Enlightened.” Dern lifts her head — she’s crying in a bathroom stall at work, having just been demoted for sleeping with the boss — and her mouth does that determined, wrenching thing only Laura Dern’s mouth can do, stretching flat like a rubber band, exposing her bottom teeth on just the right side. The mascara drips under her eyes, the lines on her forehead pop, and as two women gossip about her at the sink, the expression morphs into a grimace that carries her on a frantic rage storm through the office. Her eyes do 100 tiny calculations at once, her mouth flipping up and down and finally opening wide, wider than it should be physically possible to make a mouth, mirroring the elevator doors that she drags apart with her bare hands.', 'print_section': 'MM', 'print_page': '23', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/05/12/magazine/12mag-Dern-02/12mag-Dern-02-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 738, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2019/05/12/magazine/12mag-Dern-02/12mag-Dern-02-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 738}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/05/12/magazine/12mag-Dern-02/12mag-Dern-02-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 834, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/05/12/magazine/12mag-Dern-02/12mag-Dern-02-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1078, 'width': 877, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'ur