r de Blasio as He Weighs Presidential Run', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Ethics Cloud Hangs Over de Blasio as He Weighs Presidential Run', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'de Blasio, Bill', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Conflicts of Interest Board (NYC)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Conflicts of Interest', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Campaign Finance', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Mayors', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Baker & Hostetler LLP', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Department of Investigation (NYC)', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York City', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bohorquez, Fernando A', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Briffault, Richard', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2019-05-07T09:00:10+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By William Neuman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'William', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Neuman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/0e343c39-b81a-5ffc-8098-a14aee8b2a36', 'word_count': 1444, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0e343c39-b81a-5ffc-8098-a14aee8b2a36'}, {'abstract': 'The magazine’s Ethicist columnist on calling the cops on a black man breaking into a car and selling your condo to someone accused of sexual assault.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2019/05/07/magazine/was-i-right-to-call-the-cops-on-a-black-man-breaking-into-a-car.html', 'snippet': 'The magazine’s Ethicist columnist on calling the cops on a black man breaking into a car and selling your condo to someone accused of sexual assault.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Recently, I witnessed a young black male cut across my yard, duck between my neighbors’ two cars and try the doors of both, before “breaking” into the unlocked one. I opened my back door and yelled, “I see you getting into that car!” He took off running. I called the police and then posted to the (admittedly sometimes racially charged) Nextdoor app, in the hopes that my neighbors would check the locks on their cars and homes.', 'print_section': 'MM', 'print_page': '16', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/10/07/magazine/12mag-ethicist-image1/12mag-ethicist-image1-articleLarge-v21.jpg', 'height': 308, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2018/10/07/magazine/12mag-ethicist-image1/12mag-ethicist-image1-articleLarge-v21.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 308}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/10/07/magazine/12mag-ethicist-image1/12mag-ethicist-image1-jumbo-v21.jpg', 'height': 526, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/10/07/magazine/12mag-ethicist-image1/12mag-ethicist-image1-superJumbo-v21.jpg', 'height': 1051, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/10/07/magazine/12mag-ethicist-image1/12mag-ethicist-image1-thumbStandard-v23.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2018/10/07/magazine/12mag-ethicist-image1/12mag-ethicist-image1-thumbStandard-v23.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/10/07/magazine/12mag-ethicist-image1/12mag-ethicist-image1-thumbLarge-v23.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Was I Right to Call the Cops on a Black Man Breaking Into a Car?', 'kicker': 'The Ethicist ', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Was I Right to Call the Cops on a Black Man Breaking Into a Car?', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Blacks', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Black People', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Police Brutality, Misconduct and Shootings', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Race and Ethnicity', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Locks and Keys', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Real Estate and Housing (Residential)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Sex Crimes', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Condominiums', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2019-05-07T09:00:10+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Magazine', 'section_name': 'Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Kwame Anthony Appiah', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Kwame', 'middlename': 'Anthony', 'lastname': 'Appiah', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ff808174-f152-5ed4-a526-736226303339', 'word_count': 1453, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ff808174-f152-5ed4-a526-736226303339'}, {'abstract': 'The family behind Lisbon’s Casa Fortunato lives among — and just above — their guests.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2019/05/07/t-magazine/casa-fortunato-lisbon-hotel.html', 'snippet': 'The family behind Lisbon’s Casa Fortunato lives among — and just above — their guests.', 'lead_paragraph': 'EARLY IN THEIR RELATIONSHIP, the architect António Falcão Costa Lopes and his wife, Filipa Fortunato, decided that opening a hotel one day might stave off empty-nest syndrome. “When we got married, over 20 years ago, we noticed that our parents were sad, even a little lonely, when we moved out,” says Fortunato, now 44, adding, half-jokingly, “We thought if we had a small hotel, and lived there, we would always have guests and wouldn’t get tired of talking only to each other.” The original plan was to sell their four-bedroom apartment in Bairro das Estacas, a Modernist complex in northern Lisbon, and build a nearby house-hotel from scratch after the last of their four children left for university, an event still 13 years off. “Then fate intervened,” says Fortunato — and now the couple is looking after children and guests both.', 'print_section': 'M2', 'print_page': '66', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/05/13/t-magazine/13tmag-casafortunato-slide-7D2R/13tmag-casafortunato-slide-7D2R-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2019/05/13/t-magazine/13tmag-casafortunato-slide-7D2R/13tmag-casafortunato-slide-7D2R-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/05/13/t-magazine/13tmag-casafortunato-slide-7D2R/13tmag-casafortunato-slide-7D2R-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/05/13/t-magazine/13tmag-casafortunato-slide-7D2R/13tmag-casafortunato-slide-7D2R-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1100, 'width': 1649, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thum