on of the Saul Bellow novel is about to open in the city, and campus, that helped shape his sensibility.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2019/05/07/theater/a-new-adventure-for-augie-march-a-chicago-stage.html', 'snippet': 'A theatrical adaptation of the Saul Bellow novel is about to open in the city, and campus, that helped shape his sensibility.', 'lead_paragraph': 'CHICAGO — When “The Adventures of Augie March,” Saul Bellow’s groundbreaking 500-plus-page Chicago epic, was published in 1953, it shook up literature. For the first time, an American writer told a Jewish-American hero’s picaresque story of self-discovery in heightened language and street-smart argot. Zachary Leader, Bellow’s most recent biographer, calls it “the great American novel.”', 'print_section': 'AR', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/05/12/arts/12AUGIE1/12AUGIE1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 480, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2019/05/12/arts/12AUGIE1/12AUGIE1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 480}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/05/12/arts/12AUGIE1/12AUGIE1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 819, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/05/12/arts/12AUGIE1/12AUGIE1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1637, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/05/12/arts/12AUGIE1/12AUGIE1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2019/05/12/arts/12AUGIE1/12AUGIE1-thumbS