 “It’s frightening,” the mayor said.', 'lead_paragraph': 'GRAFTON, Ill. — The Mississippi River annexed Jerry and Sue Eller’s backyard, invaded their basement and converted their street into a boat ramp.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '13', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Midwestern Floods Pit Communities Against One Another as Levees Rise Ever Higher', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Town Embraced the River, but the River Keeps On Rising', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Floods', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Rivers', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Levees and Dams', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Mississippi River', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'GRAFTON (ILL)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Davenport (Iowa)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Midwestern States (US)', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2019-05-07T14:09:24+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Mitch Smith', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Mitch', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Smith', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/df2a14a9-87fa-5da5-b93d-c5a5348f6f47', 'word_count': 1214, 'uri': 'nyt://article/df2a14a9-87fa-5da5-b93d-c5a5348f6f47'}, {'abstract': 'The Treasury secretary is defying the law and Supreme Court precedent.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2019/05/07/opinion/trump-tax-returns-congress.html', 'snippet': 'The Treasury secretary is defying the law and Supreme Court precedent.', 'lead_paragraph': 'As to whether Congress may obtain a president’s tax returns, there is no ambiguity: Federal law empowers the chairman of the House Ways and Means Committee to submit a written request to the Treasury Department, which oversees the Internal Revenue Service, for “any return or return information.” The Treasury secretary then “shall furnish” the requested information to the committee so that it may conduct its legislative functions.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '24', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/05/07/opinion/07mnuchiWeb/merlin_153273822_0afe5cb5-9c2e-44e1-8b58-5c16a3034859-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2019/05/07/opinion/07mnuchiWeb/merlin_153273822_0afe5cb5-9c2e-44e1-8b58-5c16a3034859-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/05/07/opinion/07mnuchiWeb/merlin_153273822_0afe5cb5-9c2e-44e1-8b58-5c16a3034859-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/05/07/opinion/07mnuchiWeb/merlin_153273822_0afe5cb5-9c2e-44e1-8b58-5c16a3034859-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/05/07/opinion/07mnuchiWeb/07mnuchiWeb-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2019/05/07/opinion/07mnuchiWeb/07mnuchiWeb-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/05/07/opinion/07mnuchiWeb/07mnuchiWeb-thumbLarge.jpg'