_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/826e6df2-f49e-58b7-a6c9-74d17a368e63', 'word_count': 1043, 'uri': 'nyt://article/826e6df2-f49e-58b7-a6c9-74d17a368e63'}, {'abstract': 'The bond with my Australian cattle dog has been the most effective way for me to stay sober.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2019/05/08/opinion/alcoholics-anonymous-sobriety-dog.html', 'snippet': 'The bond with my Australian cattle dog has been the most effective way for me to stay sober.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Most nights, my dog River sleeps in my bed. He is a red heeler, although his speckled coat is closer to an auburn-bronze than any shade that could be earnestly called “red.” Before I fall asleep, he jumps onto the comforter and curls up into a furry crescent moon next to me, nuzzling his rust-colored snout into my chest and wedging himself somewhere in between my limbs and heart.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/05/11/opinion/07watamanuk/d26bcaf2db7b4bc280591a5e8f78fd87-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 720, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2019/05/11/opinion/07watamanuk/d26bcaf2db7b4bc280591a5e8f78fd87-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 720}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/05/11/opinion/07watamanuk/d26bcaf2db7b4bc280591a5e8f78fd87-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 854, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/05/11/opinion/07watamanuk/d26bcaf2db7b4bc280591a5e8f78fd87-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1707, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/05/11/opi