y for doctors to perform them.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Alabama Senate on Thursday postponed debate on a proposal to outlaw most abortions in the state, delaying a measure that is intended to serve as a direct challenge to the Supreme Court’s holding that a woman has a constitutional right to end a pregnancy.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '17', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Amid Chaos, Alabama Lawmakers Delay Vote on Far-Reaching Abortion Ban', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Uproar in Legislature Delays Alabama Vote On Strict Abortion Ban', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'ALABAMA', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'ABORTION', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Law and Legislation', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'State Legislatures', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Politics and Government', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Supreme Court (US)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Roe v Wade (Supreme Court Decision)', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2019-05-09T17:08:18+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Alan Blinder', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Alan', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Blinder', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/6e68d118-e8af-5678-91fc-7e4461d24a64', 'word_count': 1166, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6e68d118-e8af-5678-91fc-7e4461d24a64'}, {'abstract': 'The president also said he was “pretty surprised” his eldest son, Donald Trump Jr., was subpoenaed to testify before the Senate about contacts with Russians in the 2016 campaign.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2019/05/09/us/politics/mueller-testify.html', 'snippet': 'The president also said he was “pretty surprised” his eldest son, Donald Trump Jr., was subpoenaed to testify before the Senate about contacts with Russians in the 2016 campaign.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WASHINGTON — President Trump said Thursday that he would leave it to Attorney General William P. Barr to decide whether the special counsel testifies before Congress, a concession of sorts after Speaker Nancy Pelosi declared the country in a “constitutional crisis” over the president’s blanket refusal to cooperate with the Democrats investigating him.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '15', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Trump Suggests Mueller May Testify; Pelosi Declares ‘Constitutional Crisis’', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Trump’s New Position: Barr Can Decide if Mueller Testifies', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Trump, Donald J', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Mueller, Robert S III', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Special Prosecutors (Independent Counsel)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Pelosi, Nancy', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'House of Representatives', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Senate', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Presidential Election of 2016', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Russian Interference in 2016 US Elections and Ties to Trump Associates', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Barr, William P', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Trump, Donald J Jr', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Justice Department', 'rank': 11, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2019-05-09T17:09:45+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Washington', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Annie Karni and Sheryl Gay Stolberg', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Annie', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Karni', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Sheryl', 'middlename': 'Gay', 'lastname': 'Stolberg', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/5c0ca9bf-acaa-5807-90b3-0e623bf54b73', 'word_count': 1156, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5c0ca9bf-acaa-5807-90b3-0e623bf54b73'}, {'abstract': 'His struggles to complete a book caught the eye of one of his students, Michael Chabon. Some years later, he finished the book, “Honeymooners.”', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2019/05/09/obituaries/chuck-kinder-dead.html', 'snippet': 'His struggles to complete a book caught the eye of one of his students, Michael Chabon. Some years later, he finished the book, “Honeymooners.”', 'lead_paragraph': 'Chuck Kinder, who turned his friendship with Raymond Carver into a roman à clef, and whose long struggle to birth that book inspired a novel by one of his former students, Michael Chabon, died on May 3 in South Miami, Fla. He was 76.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '28', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/05/12/obituaries/12kinder-obit1/24912937fbef4bcfab3a54dff061d760-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 399, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2019/05/12/obituaries/12kinder-obit1/24912937fbef4bcfab3a54dff061d760-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 399}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/05/12/obituaries/12kinder-obit1/24912937fbef4bcfab3a54dff061d760-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 680, 'width': 10