le': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Kate', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Conger', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d275c69a-cfd4-5cd4-95e8-3d216a092f77', 'word_count': 714, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d275c69a-cfd4-5cd4-95e8-3d216a092f77'}, {'abstract': 'After years of picking my skin bloody, I’ve finally found (and stuck to) a routine that anyone can follow.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2019/05/09/smarter-living/skin-picking-affordable-skin-care-mental-health.html', 'snippet': 'After years of picking my skin bloody, I’ve finally found (and stuck to) a routine that anyone can follow.', 'lead_paragraph': 'I needed to be out the door 15 minutes ago for a friend’s bachelorette party — or was it 30 minutes ago? Instead, I sat cross-legged on the floor before a closet mirror, picking and squeezing and scratching my face — thinking that if I could just “get this gunk out,” I’d be able to quell my anxiety and leave the apartment. I wasn’t sure how much time had passed, but when I finally surveyed the damage, my face was bloody, swollen, and hot to the touch. In a trance-like state, I’d been digging at my skin for an hour and half.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/03/22/smarter-living/00sl_skincare/00sl_skincare-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 685, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2019/03/22/smarter-living/00sl_skincare/00sl_skincare-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 685}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/03/22/smarter-living/00sl_skincare/00sl_skincare-jumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 897, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy':