d his own willingness to share it with his audience.', 'lead_paragraph': '“The only thing weirder than finding out your father has a second family — is finding out that you guys are that second family.”', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/05/13/arts/13carmichael1-promo/13carmichael1-promo-articleLarge-v3.jpg', 'height': 450, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2019/05/13/arts/13carmichael1-promo/13carmichael1-promo-articleLarge-v3.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 450}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/05/13/arts/13carmichael1-promo/13carmichael1-promo-jumbo-v3.jpg', 'height': 768, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/05/13/arts/13carmichael1-promo/13carmichael1-promo-superJumbo-v3.jpg', 'height': 1536, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/05/13/arts/13carmichael1-promo/13carmichael1-promo-thumbStandard-v3.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2019/05/13/arts/13carmichael1-promo/13carmichael1-promo-thumbStandard-v3.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/05/13/arts/13carmichael1-promo/13carmichael1-promo-thumbLarge-v3.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Jerrod Carmichael Is Ready to Get Personal (to a Degree)', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Jerrod Carmichael Gets Personal', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Television', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Carmichael, Jerrod', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'Home Videos (TV Program)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Home Box Office', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2019-05-13T09:00:11+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Television', 'byline': {'original': 'By Aisha Harris', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Aisha', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Harris', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ab682181-fbdb-564c-9e51-44b005c9d97c', 'word_count': 1641, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ab682181-fbdb-564c-9e51-44b005c9d97c'}, {'abstract': 'From Athens to Ithaca, a guide to journeying through classical antiquity — and enjoying a few modern comforts along the way.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2019/05/13/t-magazine/travel/greece-travel-guide-athens-nafplio-ithaca.html', 'snippet': 'From Athens to Ithaca, a guide to journeying through classical antiquity — and enjoying a few modern comforts along the way.', 'lead_paragraph': 'While many countries still bare traces of the ancient civilizations they once fostered, in Greece, antiquity can feel especially tangible. “It’s the absence of modern developments — of high-rises and high-speed technologies — that can make you feel as if you’re walking among the ancient philosophers and tragedians who gave us our sense of hubris and catharsis,” writes Pico Iyer in his story for T’s spring Travel issue, for which he journeyed to some of the country’s most storied classical sites. Retracing a route he’d traveled some 35 years before, Iyer made his way from the sprawling metropolis of Athens to the ancient city of Mycenae and the sacred sanctuary at Epidaurus, then on to the sleepy port town of Nafplio and finally to Ithaca, the island Odysseus reputedly called home. Here, a practical guide to making a similar pilgrimage across the Peloponnese, with ideas for where to stay and what to eat and drink.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/05/13/t-magazine/13tmag-greece-01/9abf64615b6f4ae9bc9166d736cd60cb-1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 809, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2019/05/13/t-magazine/13tmag-greece-01/9abf64615b6f4ae9bc9166d736cd60cb-1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 809}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/05/13/t-magazine/13tmag-greece-01/9abf64615b6f4ae9bc9166d736cd60cb-1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 760, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/05/13/t-magazine/13tmag-greece-01/9abf64615b6f4ae9bc9166d736cd60cb-1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2000, 'width': 1483, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/05/13/t-magazine/13tmag-greece-01/13tmag-greece-01-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2019/05/13/t-magazine/13tmag-greece-01/13tmag-greece-01-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/05/13/t-magazine/13tmag-greece-01/13tmag-greece-01-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'How to Visit the Most Storied Sites of Ancient Greece', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Greek Civilization', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Greek Food (Cuisine)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Travel and Vacations', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Athens (Greece)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Epidaurus (Greece)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Ithaca (NY)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2019-05-13T09:00:13+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'TStyle', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'subsection_name': 'Travel', 'byline': {'original': 'By Michaela Trimble', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Michaela', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Trimble', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/6f674cc7-7475-56ed-91ac-6c5cb24503c6', 'word_count': 1766, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6f674cc7-7475-56ed-91ac-6c5cb24503c6'}, {'abstract': 'One writer chronicles his voyage to the island of Ithaca, where Odysseus was once reputedly king.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2019/05/13/t-magazine/greece-ithaca-visit.html', 'snippet': 'One writer chronicles his voyage to the island of Ithaca, where Odysseus was once reputedly king.', 'lead_paragraph': 'I STEPPED INTO a taxi on my arrival in Athens and mentioned the name of one of the city’s most central five-star hotels. The driver was thrown into a frenzy, and not only because he seemed to speak no English. As we zigzagged at high speed through the jampacked streets, he tapped frantically on his smartphone and started calling friends, none of whom were any help at all. When, finally, we pulled up at the entrance, I was greeted by a wild-haired, gesticulating front-desk man who said, “We’re so sorry, sir. We have a problem, a big problem, today. So we have made a reservation for you in our other hotel. Half a block away.”', 'print_section': 'M2', 'print_page': '136', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/05/01/t-magazine/oakImage-1556722663967/oakImage-1556722663967-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 449, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2019/05/01/t-magazine/oakImage-1556722663967/oakImage-1556722663967-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 449}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/05/01/t-magazine/oakImage-1556722663967/oakImage-1556722663967-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 766, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/05/01/t-magazine/oakImage-1556722663967/oakImage-1556722663967-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1533, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/05/01/t-magazine/oakImage-1556722663967/oakImage-1556722663967-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2019/05/01/t-magazine/oakImage-1556722663967/oakImage-1556722663967-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/05/01/t-magazine/oakImage-1556722663967/oakImage-1556722663967-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'A Journey Into Greece’s Land of a Thousand Stories', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'In the Realm of The Gods', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Greek Civilization', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Plato (428-348 BC)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Greece', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Athens (Greece)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Homer', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'MOUNT ATHOS (GREECE)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2019-05-13T09:00:14+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'TStyle', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Pico Iyer', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Pico', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Iyer', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/be064c18-e134-5bb7-91b2-e6d0d4215135', 'word_count': 2836, 'uri': 'nyt://article/be064c18-e134-5bb7-91b2-e6d0d4215135'}, {'abstract': 'With a barely-4-year-old and a not-quite-2-year-old, in a 32-foot boat sailing up the Inside Passage, a family discovers the best rewards are those never imagined.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2019/05/13/travel/alaska-family-sailing-inside-passage.html', 'snippet': 'With a barely-4-year-old and a not-quite-2-year-old, in a 32-foot boat sailing up the Inside Passage, a family discovers the best rewards are those never imagined.', 'lead_paragraph': 'This was the third time I’d sailed up the Inside Passage in a boat. The third time I’d watched surf explode from the rocky headlands of northern Vancouver Island, the swell rhythmically shifting my view of the horizon. The umpteenth time I’d listened to the weather forecast on the VHF radio while g