https://www.nytimes.com/2019/05/13/opinion/roe-supreme-court.html', 'snippet': 'Conservatives may be laying the foundation for the reversal of the landmark abortion decision.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Supreme Court made clear on Monday that Roe v. Wade may soon no longer be the law of the land. The decision, Franchise Tax Board of California v. Hyatt, actually has nothing to do with abortion; it concerns when one state may be sued in another state’s courts.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '23', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/05/14/opinion/14litman/14litman-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2019/05/14/opinion/14litman/14litman-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/05/14/opinion/14litman/14litman-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/05/14/opinion/14litman/14litman-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/05/14/opinion/14litman/14litman-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2019/05/14/opinion/14litman/14litman-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/05/14/opinion/14litman/14litman-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Supreme Court Liberals Raise Alarm Bells About Roe v. Wade', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Scary Sign That Roe  Is at Risk', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'ABORTION', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Constitution (US)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Roe v Wade (Supreme Court Decision)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Supreme Court (US)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'United States', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Breyer, Stephen G', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Hyatt, Gilbert P', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2019-05-13T23:00:04+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Leah Litman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Leah', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Litman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/62abc0ef-4a1c-5cf7-baf9-e32d0052401a', 'word_count': 913, 'uri': 'nyt://article/62abc0ef-4a1c-5cf7-baf9-e32d0052401a'}, {'abstract': 'The havoc caused by stocking the park’s lake for sport fishing ravaged ospreys, pelicans, bald eagles, grizzly bears and the lake’s own native cutthroat trout.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2019/05/13/opinion/fishing-species-extinction-yellowstone.html', 'snippet': 'The havoc caused by stocking the park’s lake for sport fishing ravaged ospreys, pelicans, bald eagles, grizzly bears and the lake’s own native cutthroat trout.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Recreational fishing is a pastime in which people have come to expect the fish they want in the places they happen to want them. That is, they want their fish stocked and ready to catch, even in places those fish never originally lived. This practice can seem harmless, or even beneficial. But the introduction of one “beneficial” species in Yellowstone National Park suggests how rejiggering the natural world for human convenience can cause ecological disaster for almost everything else.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '23', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/05/15/opinion/13conniff/merlin_154798068_576b1acc-72f1-4d23-922c-d08023284391-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 720, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2019/05/15/opinion/13conniff/merlin_154798068_576b1acc-72f1-4d23-922c-d08023284391-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 720}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/05/15/opinion/13conniff/merlin_154798068_576b1acc-72f1-4d23-922c-d08023284391-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 854, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/05/15/opinion/13conniff/merlin_154798068_576b1acc-72f1-4d23-922c-d08023284391-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1707, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/05/15/opinion/13conniff/13conniff-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2019/05/15/opinion/13conniff/13conniff-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/05/15/opinion/13conniff/13conniff-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop