asts.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Drink-specific cocktail glasses are nothing new — who doesn’t recognize a rocks glass? — but the Austrian glassware company Riedel has taken it a step further, consulting with Zane Harris, a cocktail specialist, to fine-tune the details for each of the six shapes in a new line. The glasses follow classic contours, yet also take ice (regular and large format cubes) into consideration. There’s a 6 1/2-ounce glass for neat whiskey, a 9 7/8-ounce rocks glass, a 10 7/8-ounce highball, a slightly narrower 9 3/8-ounce tall fizz glass, a 7 5/8-ounce sour glass and a 4 7/8-ounce glass called the Nick & Nora that’s meant for martinis, but isn’t the typical “V” shape. All are comfortable in the hand and make for easy sipping.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/05/15/dining/13burner3/merlin_153379953_77c25139-1a74-4f50-bd53-f33c94be8733-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2019/05/15/dining/13burner3/merlin_153379953_77c25139-1a74-4f50-bd53-f33c94be8733-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/05/15/dining/13burner3/merlin_153379953_77c25139-1a74-4f50-bd53-f33c94be8733-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/05/15/dining/13burner3/merlin_153379953_77c25139-1a74-4f50-bd53-f33c94be8733-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/05/15/dining/13burner3/13burner3-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2019/05/15/dining/13burner3/13burner3-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/05/15/dining/13burner3/13burner3-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'A Better Cocktail Glass', 'kicker': 'Front Burner', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'To Fill: Nick and Nora Would Likely Approve', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Glassware', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Riedel Crystal', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Harris, Zane', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2019-05-13T23:45:17+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Dining', 'section_name': 'Food', 'subsection_name': 'Wine, Beer & Cocktails', 'byline': {'original': 'By Florence Fabricant', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Florence', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Fabricant', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/5eb49c25-f277-5317-b484-2025c3d99070', 'word_count': 159, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5eb49c25-f277-5317-b484-2025c3d99070'}, {'abstract': 'The cottage cheesemaker Good Culture has a new offering along with a sour cream.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2019/05/13/dining/good-culture-cottage-cheese.html', 'snippet': 'The cottage cheesemaker Good Culture has a new offering along with a sour cream.', 'lead_paragraph': 'With cottage cheese no longer sidelined as a diet food, there are now many examples that are better quality, without gums and additives, made from milk from small farms and often organic. Good Culture is a brand that fits that description. The four-year-old California company uses milk from pastured animals in the Midwest and has organic and nonorganic products. It has now added a double-cream small-curd cottage cheese and has introduced a rich sour cream.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/05/15/dining/13burner1/13burner1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 528, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2019/05/15/dining/13burner1/13burner1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 528}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/05/15/dining/13burner1/13burner1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 901, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/05/15/dining/13burner1/13burner1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1802, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/05/15/dining/13burner1/13burner1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2019/05/15/dining/13burner1/13burner1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/05/15/dining/13burner1/13burner1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'More Flavor From a Cottage Cheese', 'kicker': 'Front Burner', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'To Spoon: In the Pursuit Of Free-Range Curds', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cooking and Cookbooks', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Dairy Products', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Good Culture LLC', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2019-05-13T23:48:25+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Dining', 'section_name': 'Food', 'byline': {'original': 'By Florence Fabricant', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Florence', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Fabricant', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/08eb312b-6999-5f28-a147-5b3cc9f9884c', 'word_count': 125, 'uri': 'nyt://article/08eb312b-6999-5f28-a147-5b3cc9f9884c'}, {'abstract': 'Inspired by an Indonesian street snack, this appetizer from Cédric Vongerichten is easy to whip up at home.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2019/05/13/dining/wayan-corn-fritters.html', 'snippet': 'Inspired by an Indonesian street snack, this appetizer from Cédric Vongerichten is easy to whip up at home.', 'lead_paragraph': 'They’re listed on the menu as a side dish, but the corn fritters at Wayan, the new Indonesian restaurant co-owned by Cédric Vongerichten, deserve marquee billing. Crunchy, sweet, spicy and irresistible, it is a typical Indonesian snack, according to Ochi Latjuba Vongerichten, Mr. Vongerichten’s wife and a partner in the restaurant, who is from Jakarta. Try this at home: Whisk together three-quarters cup of all-purpose flour, a quarter cup of rice flour, a teaspoon-and-a-half of baking powder and a half-teaspoon, or more, of salt. Mix in two-thirds cup water, then fold in 10 ounces of fresh or frozen corn kernels (almost two cups), two scallions, minced, and a finely chopped Fresno or jalapeño chile. In a sauté pan or cast-iron skillet, heat an inch of vegetable oil, such as grapeseed, to 375 degrees. For 16 medium-size fritters, drop batter by heaping tablespoons into hot oil, flatten slightly and fry, turning once, until well browned. Drain on paper towels before serving. For eight large ones, as they are served in the restaurant, use about a half-cup of batter for each and flatten them. Scallions, cilantro and fried shallots are typical toppings.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/05/15/dining/13burner2/merlin_153540624_2949feed-be1f-41e4-9e25-f9071d7d038c-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2019/05/15/dining/13burner2/merlin_153540624_2949feed-be1f-41e4-9e25-f9071d7d038c-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/05/15/dining/13burner2/merlin_153540624_2949feed-be1f-41e4-9e25-f9071d7d038c-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/05/15/dining/13burner2/merlin_153540624_2949feed-be1f-41e4-9e25-f9071d7d038c-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/05/15/dining/13burner2/13burner2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2019/05/15/dining/13burner2/13burner2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/05/15/dining/13burner2/13burner2-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Make the Corn Fritters From Wayan', 'kicker': 'Front Burner', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'To Munch: An Excellent Way To Fritter Time Away', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cooking and Cookbooks', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Restaurants', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Corn', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Wayan (Manhattan, NY, Restaurant)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Vongerichten, Cedric', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2019-05-13T23:50:02+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Dining', 'section_name': 'Food', 'byline': {'original': 'By Florence Fabricant', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Florence', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Fabricant', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/8c1169b7-8b17-5844-8506-a0e413d68950', 'word_count': 226, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8c1169b7-8b17-5844-8506-a0e413d68950'}, {'abstract': 'After Hicks returned from a two-month absence, Andujar and Jonathan Loaisiga were placed on the injury list.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2019/05/13/sports/yankees-aaron-hicks-miguel-andujar.html', 'snippet': 'After Hicks returned from a two-month absence, Andujar and Jonathan Loaisiga were placed on the injury list.', 'lead_paragraph': 'When it comes to injuries this season, every Yankee step forward seems to be accompanied by two backward.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '12', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/05/14/business/14YANKEESprint1/merlin_151245114_c6b0d9c8-b9e6-4d76-a6f6-8b17a0b27420-articleLarge.j