rin', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/e4b8c318-5102-510c-9c43-71b9b09306d1', 'word_count': 1817, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e4b8c318-5102-510c-9c43-71b9b09306d1'}, {'abstract': 'The chief theater critics for The Times choose who they think should win and who should have been nominated.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2019/05/14/theater/tony-awards-critics-picks.html', 'snippet': 'The chief theater critics for The Times choose who they think should win and who should have been nominated.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Ben Brantley and Jesse Green, the chief theater critics for The New York Times, make their Tony Award choices. For the Should Have Been Nominated category, they were allowed to expand the potential nominees to productions ineligible for the Tonys, including those Off Broadway, which are designated by an asterisk.', 'print_section': 'AR', 'print_page': '27', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/05/19/arts/19critic-ballot3/19critic-ballot3-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 412, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2019/05/19/arts/19critic-ballot3/19critic-ballot3-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 412}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/05/19/arts/19critic-ballot3/19critic-ballot3-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 703, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/05/19/arts/19critic-ballot3/19critic-ballot3-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1406, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None