'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/05/19/books/review/17Winchester/17Winchester-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'How Was Polynesia Populated? Two New Books Explore the Pacific’s Mysteries', 'kicker': 'Nonfiction', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Aloha', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Maori', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Indigenous Australians', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Easter Island', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'French Polynesia (France)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Hawaii', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New Zealand', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'Endeavour (Book)', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2019-05-14T09:00:09+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'BookReview', 'section_name': 'Books', 'subsection_name': 'Book Review', 'byline': {'original': 'By Simon Winchester', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Simon', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Winchester', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/1ecaa1e7-0239-5545-9309-f7fb280c9d69', 'word_count': 1901, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1ecaa1e7-0239-5545-9309-f7fb280c9d69'}, {'abstract': 'Capturing one incredible piece in the middle of its creation. This month: a collar meant to resemble an exploding nebula.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2019/05/14/t-magazine/cartier-necklace-making-of.html', 'snippet': 'Capturing one incredible piece in the middle of its creation. This month: a collar meant to resemble an exploding nebula.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The making of a one-of-kind high jewelry piece often begins with a hunt for extraordinary stones. In the case of this recently completed elaborate collar by the Paris-based Cartier, that expedition began and ended at the annual gem show in Tucson, Ariz. While there are other such trade events throughout the world — Hong Kong, Basel, Switzerland, and Las Vegas also host prominent events — the Tucson show is the most idiosyncratic, with dealers bringing crystals, minerals and fossils in addition to precious and semiprecious stones. The six-person Cartier team spotted the more-than-15-carat octagonal yellow sapphire at a booth on the first day and a few hours later connected with a dealer who had a cache of brilliant blue lapis lazuli beads. Though purchases from a particular trip don’t always end up in the same piece, in this instance, the jewelers were struck by how the contrasting hues of pale orangy-yellow and intense cobalt might work together, echoing past Cartier collections that paired blue stones with gold.', 'print_section': 'M2', 'print_page': '104', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/05/14/t-magazine/14tmag-cartier-copy/14tmag-cartier-copy-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2019/05/14/t-magazine/14tmag-cartier-copy/14tmag-cartier-copy-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/05/14/t-magazine/14tmag-cartier-copy/14tmag-cartier-copy-jumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/05/14/t-magazine/14tmag-cartier-copy/14tmag-cartier-copy-superJumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 1258, 'width': 1887, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/05/14/t-magazine/14tmag-cartier-copy/14tmag-cartier-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2019/05/14/t-magazine/14tmag-cartier-copy/14tmag-cartier-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/05/14/t-magazine/14tmag-cartier-copy/14tmag-cartier-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'It Took More Than 40 Days to Make This Cartier Necklace', 'kicker': 'Rough Draft', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Cartier Necklace', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Jewels and Jewelry', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Gold', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Cartier SA', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Paris (France)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2019-05-14T09:00:09+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'TStyle', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Nancy Hass', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Nancy', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Hass', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/93d4bac7-c431-5bd0-aff4-7f81fdf6f3ab', 'word_count': 434, 'uri': 'nyt://article/93d4bac7-c431-5bd0-aff4-7f81fdf6f3ab'}, {'abstract': 'In the spring, a.k.a. mud season, the mountains are beautiful, the hotel rooms are half price and the $2 draft beers are flowing.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2019/05/14/travel/colorado-ski-resorts-cheap.html', 'snippet': 'In the spring, a.k.a. mud season, the mountains are beautiful, the hotel rooms are half price and the $2 draft beers are flowing.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The weekend before Christmas, a night at the Ritz Carlton Bachelor Gulch, the luxurious hotel at the center of the Beaver Creek Ski Resort in Colorado, costs $1,489. In July, it goes for $659. But on a recent Saturday night, my wife and I paid just $189 for a similar room. We had to add $30 for valet parking, but breakfast was free and with spa treatments half-price, we spent only $80 for a half-hour in a copper bathtub-for-two, which included champagne, robes, slippers and tinkly new-age music.', 'print_section': 'TR', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/05/19/travel/15-frugal-off-season-ski1/merlin_154426275_02ad1dd7-3845-4bff-b70e-75275eb71e65-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 450, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2019/05/19/travel/15-frugal-off-season-ski1/merlin_154426275_02ad1dd7-3845-4bff-b70e-75275eb71e65-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 450}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/05/19/travel/15-frugal-off-season-ski1/merlin_154426275_02ad1dd7-3845-4bff-b70e-75275eb71e65-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 768, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/05/19/travel/15-frugal-off-season-ski1/merlin_154426275_02ad1dd7-3845-4bff-b70e-75275eb71e65-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1536, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'i