culture. ', 'lead_paragraph': 'Our columnist, Sebastian Modak, is visiting each destination on our 52 Places to Go in 2019 list. He went camping and scuba diving in Israel before heading to Plovdiv.', 'print_section': 'TR', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/05/14/travel/14PTG-Bulgaria2-promo/14PTG-Bulgaria2-promo-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2019/05/14/travel/14PTG-Bulgaria2-promo/14PTG-Bulgaria2-promo-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/05/14/travel/14PTG-Bulgaria2-promo/14PTG-Bulgaria2-promo-jumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/05/14/travel/14PTG-Bulgaria2-promo/14PTG-Bulgaria2-promo-superJumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/05/14/travel/14PTG-Bulgaria2-promo/14PTG-Bulgaria2-promo-thumbStandard-v3.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2019/05/14/travel/14PTG-Bulgaria2-promo/14PTG-Bulgaria2-promo-thumbStandard-v3.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/05/14/travel/14PTG-Bulgaria2-promo/14PTG-Bulgaria2-promo-thumbLarge-v3.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Roman Ruins? Sure, but Bulgaria’s Second City Offers So Much More', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'So Much More Than Roman Ruins', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2019-05-14T09:00:14+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Travel', 'section_name': 'Travel', 'byline': {'original': 'By Sebastian Modak', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Sebastian', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Modak', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/59d876cd-95d5-5427-80b0-19346e2d2df2', 'word_count': 2120, 'uri': 'nyt://article/59d876cd-95d5-5427-80b0-19346e2d2df2'}, {'abstract': 'It’s liberating to see bones as mere décor.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2019/05/14/magazine/letter-of-recommendation-catacombs.html', 'snippet': 'It’s liberating to see bones as mere décor.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In 18th-century Paris, there were a lot of dead bodies and a limited amount of space to bury them, and eventually the city ran out of ground. The graves held so many dead that bodies burst through people’s basements. I once heard on a walking tour that Parisians who lived near these pre-catacomb graveyards couldn’t keep milk — it would spoil within hours. The bacteria in the air, from proximity to so much rotting flesh, would also turn wine. Catholicism forbade cremation, and crypts were already a public-health nightmare, so the only place to go was down. Burials within city limits were finally banned in 1780, after two decades of attempts. In 1785, the effort to remove human remains from graveyards and transfer them to underground tunnels was made law. That year, an old limestone mine was turned into an ossuary, and the city began moving all the bones there.', 'print_section': 'MM', 'print_page': '16', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/05/19/magazine/19mag-LOR/6d8461ef352747ba9dc17b41c5e80f27-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 437, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2019/05/19/magazine/19mag-LOR/6d8461ef352747ba9dc17b41c5e80f27-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 437}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/05/19/magazine/19mag-LOR/6d8461ef352747ba9dc17b41c5e80f27-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 745, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/05/19/magazine/19mag-LOR/6d8461ef352747ba9dc17b41c5e80f27-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1490, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/05/19/magazine/19mag-LOR/6d8461ef352747ba9dc17b41c5e80f27-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2019/05/19/magazine/19mag-LOR/6d8461ef352747ba9dc17b41c5e80f27-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/05/19/magazine/19mag-LOR/6d8461ef352747ba9dc17b41c5e80f27-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Letter of Recommendation: Catacombs', 'kicker': 'Letter of Recommendation', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Catacombs', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Skeletons', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Bones', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Travel and Vacations', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'n