'', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Obituary (Obit)', '_id': 'nyt://article/f2cec30f-ca93-5d60-bca2-7c3eddd74933', 'word_count': 743, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f2cec30f-ca93-5d60-bca2-7c3eddd74933'}, {'abstract': 'A potential thaw in trade relations with Canada, Mexico and Europe comes as tension between the United States and China grows.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2019/05/15/us/politics/mnuchin-senate-nafta-steel-aluminum-tariffs.html', 'snippet': 'A potential thaw in trade relations with Canada, Mexico and Europe comes as tension between the United States and China grows.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WASHINGTON — The White House has decided to delay for six months a decision due Friday about whether to impose levies on foreign cars and car parts, people familiar with the situation said. Such a move would have taken aim at Japan and Europe, big auto manufacturers, and likely disrupted trade talks that the Trump administration had just begun.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '5', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'White House Reassesses Auto Tariffs as It Focuses on China Fight', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Auto Tariffs Put Off for 6 Months', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'International Trade and World Market', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Politics and Government', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Politics and Government', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Customs (Tariff)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'North American Free Trade Agreement', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Steel and Iron', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2019-05-15T17:06:08+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': '