: None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'David', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Gonzalez', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/41c801f9-1053-5dbe-965b-d29cf8af3874', 'word_count': 642, 'uri': 'nyt://article/41c801f9-1053-5dbe-965b-d29cf8af3874'}, {'abstract': 'With the new comedy from Olivia Wilde, the movie mainstream is finally ready to tell jubilant stories about teenagers who happen to be lesbians.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2019/05/16/movies/booksmart-lesbian-teenagers.html', 'snippet': 'With the new comedy from Olivia Wilde, the movie mainstream is finally ready to tell jubilant stories about teenagers who happen to be lesbians.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Jokes about masturbation, crushing on a cool girl from afar, messy first sexual experiences, bodily fluids in places they shouldn’t be, porn in places it shouldn’t be. Olivia Wilde’s directing debut “Booksmart” has many of the moments we’ve come to expect from a gross-out high school comedy, except this time, the teenager on a merry quest for sexual discovery is a lesbian.', 'print_section': 'AR', 'print_page': '33', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/05/19/arts/19booksmart-essay-hp/8b90f3a39c0a427087d6d0d5b4112704-articleLarge.png', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2019/05/19/arts/19booksmart-essay-hp/8b90f3a39c0a427087d6d0d5b4112704-articleLarge.png', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/05/19/arts/19booksmart-essay-hp/8b90f3a39c0a427087d6d0d5b4112704-jumbo.png', 'height': 682, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/05/19/arts/19booksmart-essay-hp/8b90f3a39c0a427087d6d0d5b4112704-superJumbo.png', 'height': 1217, 'width': 1826, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/05/19/arts/19booksmart-essay-hp/19booksmart-essay-illo-web-thumbStandard.png', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2019/05/19/arts/19booksmart-essay-hp/19booksmart-essay-illo-web-thumbStandard.png', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/05/19/arts/19booksmart-essay-hp/19booksmart-essay-illo-web-thumbLarge.png', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': '‘Booksmart’ and How Hollywood Stopped Fearing Lesbian Teens', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Young, Lesbian and Seen', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Movies', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Dever, Kaitlyn', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Wilde, Olivia', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'Booksmart (Movie)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Teenagers and Adolescence', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Homosexuality and Bisexuality', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Caplan, Lizzy', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Women and Girls', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Dating and Relationships', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2019-05-16T08:00:01+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Arts&Leisure', 'section_name': 'Movies', 'byline': {'original': 'By Eleanor Stanford', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Eleanor', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Stanford', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ce94309d-b251-5e3d-a899-fcce50d34aff', 'word_count': 1256, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ce94309d-b251-5e3d-a899-fcce50d34aff'}, {'abstract': 'Appropriately, the first-time feature filmmaker has made a movie about not judging others on appearances: It’s the raucous critical hit “Booksmart.”', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2019/05/16/movies/olivia-wilde-booksmart.html', 'snippet': 'Appropriately, the first-time feature filmmaker has made a movie about not judging others on appearances: It’s the raucous critical hit “Booksmart.”', 'lead_paragraph': 'Before Olivia Wilde was a first-time feature director or the star of innumerable projects that she was told would make her the Next Big Thing, she was one more Hollywood newcomer looking for guidance. It was in this unsettled period when Wilde, then around 20, spotted Tilda Swinton at a Golden Globes party, sidled up to her ethereal, chameleonic heroine and awkwardly asked for advice.', 'print_section': 'AR', 'print_page': '31', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/05/19/arts/19olivia-wilde/merlin_154552386_ee5f5f00-4bb6-4664-b82c-d00bc38f34ad-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 750, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2019/05/19/arts/19olivia-wilde/merlin_154552386_ee5f5f00-4bb6-4664-b82c-d00bc38f34ad-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 750}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/05/19/arts/19olivia-wilde/merlin_154552386_ee5f5f00-4bb6-4664-b82c-d00bc38f