ency)', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Bharatiya Janata Party', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2019-05-16T09:00:16+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Peter S. Goodman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Peter', 'middlename': 'S.', 'lastname': 'Goodman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/3d04cddb-c8e0-527a-92f3-a7ba1140676f', 'word_count': 1597, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3d04cddb-c8e0-527a-92f3-a7ba1140676f'}, {'abstract': 'In a region known for extremes, a newcomer to wine tastings explores a largely experimental and free-spirited vineyard scene.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2019/05/16/travel/arizona-wine-trail-verde-valley-sedona.html', 'snippet': 'In a region known for extremes, a newcomer to wine tastings explores a largely experimental and free-spirited vineyard scene.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Driving up Interstate 17 from Scottsdale, the road to Cornville flattens out over arid, vast distances where, seemingly, not much grows beyond cactus. But that vision of Arizona as a sun-baked no-man’s land is far from true. In Northern Arizona’s Yavapai County, the story is, in fact, much colder and wetter. In late March, the sunset had soaked the sky orange. There was no breeze, but continue north, and that might change. At a roadside BBQ house in Black Canyon City, the waitress told me a blizzard blew through a week before. “You’ve got good timing,” she winked, while my boyfriend and I shared a slice of homemade blueberry pie, and breathed a sigh of relief.', 'print_section': 'TR', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/05/19/travel/14Arizona-Wine-Trail6/merlin_154008360_9e8ad636-1714-4d56-bc8c-160cb7675