753efad39c', 'word_count': 513, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7ac56ff4-b028-53ee-8ecf-fe753efad39c'}, {'abstract': 'Johnny Depp rages (and raves) against the dying of the light in Wayne Roberts’s tired depiction of cancer as a liberating force.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2019/05/16/movies/the-professor-review.html', 'snippet': 'Johnny Depp rages (and raves) against the dying of the light in Wayne Roberts’s tired depiction of cancer as a liberating force.', 'lead_paragraph': 'At the start of “The Professor,” a glib portrait about a dying academic, the title character, Richard (Johnny Depp), receives a diagnosis of stage-four lung cancer; without treatment, he has probably six months to live. His plan to tell his family is upstaged after, in a single evening at the dinner table, his daughter (Odessa Young) comes out and his wife (Rosemarie DeWitt) reveals that she’s having an affair with his university’s chancellor (Ron Livingston).', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '10', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/05/16/arts/16theprofessor/merlin_154785423_c11bcc7f-f191-42d6-b2df-4e42b3d92ba2-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2019/05/16/arts/16theprofessor/merlin_154785423_c11bcc7f-f191-42d6-b2df-4e42b3d92ba2-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/05/16/arts/16theprofessor/merlin_154785423_c11bcc7f-f191-42d6-b2df-4e42b3d92ba2-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/05/16/arts/16theprofessor/merlin_154785423_c11bcc7f-f191-42d6-b2df-4e42b3d92ba2-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'wi