ajor': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2019-05-16T14:00:04+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Arts&Leisure', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Music', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jon Pareles', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jon', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Pareles', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/4038664b-4b09-52ce-ba43-5f16cacb1fcc', 'word_count': 1957, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4038664b-4b09-52ce-ba43-5f16cacb1fcc'}, {'abstract': 'Fifty years into his stage career, André De Shields cherishes the ability to change what is to come.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2019/05/16/theater/hadestown-andre-de-shields.html', 'snippet': 'Fifty years into his stage career, André De Shields cherishes the ability to change what is to come.', 'lead_paragraph': 'You could romanticize it as a balcony, but really it’s an ornate fire escape, painted creamy beige and stretched across the facade of the Walter Kerr Theater. And if you’d glanced up from West 48th Street early one evening this month, you’d have spied a tableau of considerable glamour and grace: André De Shields, in citrus-striped coat and zebra-striped shoes, posing for the camera with the animate aplomb of a model who just happens to be a dancer.', 'print_section': 'AR', 'print_page': '20', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/05/19/arts/19deshields-oak3/merlin_154633725_85e25698-a45a-416a-acd7-e3799c06438a-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 480, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2019/05/19/arts/19deshields-oak3/merlin_154633725_85e25698-a45a-416a-acd7-e3799c06438a-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 480}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/05/19/arts/19deshields-oak3/merlin_154633725_85e25698-a45a-416a-acd7-e3799c06438a-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 819, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/05/19/arts/19deshields-oak3/merlin_154633725_85e25698-a45a-416a-acd7-e3799c06438a-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1638, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/05/19/arts/19deshields-oak3/19deshields-oak3-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2019/05/19/arts/19deshields-oak3/19deshields-oak3-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/05/19/arts/19deshields-oak3/19deshields-oak3-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'He Takes Us to the Underworld in ‘Hadestown.’ And We’re Glad to Go.', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Messenger Of Grace, Now a God', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Theater', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'ACTORS AND ACTRESSES', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Tony Awards (Theater Awards)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Kerr, Walter, Theater', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'De Shields, Andre', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Chavkin, Rachel', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Mitchell, Anais', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Noblezada, Eva', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2019-05-16T14:00:06+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Arts&Leisure', 'section_name': 'Theater', 'byline': {'original': 'By Laura Collins-Hughes', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Laura', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Collins-Hughes', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c40b8e94-ae68-5ea6-802e-8e50e90e5281', 'word_count': 1454, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c40b8e94-ae68-5ea6-802e-8e50e90e5281'}, {'abstract': 'Josh Smith’s Reaper paintings; David Taylor and Marcos Ramírez ERRE’s border markers; and Alina Tenser’s shape-shifting boxes.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2019/05/16/arts/design/new-york-art-galleries-what-to-see-right-now.html', 'snippet': 'Josh Smith’s Reaper paintings; David Taylor and Marcos Ramírez ERRE’s border markers; and Alina Tenser’s shape-shifting boxes.', 'lead_paragraph': 'As a painter, Josh Smith can be an infuriating contradiction in terms. He is a passionate cynic, an artist who degrades and celebrates his medium through the relentless yet fervent repetition of a selected motif. Mr. Smith tends to work fast and a trifle sloppily, until a certain image becomes second nature, a template. This automatism opens the door to incessant variations in brushwork, background and, above all, color — as well as our consideration of same.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '17', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/05/16/arts/16galleries-smith/16galleries-smith-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2019/05/16/arts/16galleries-smith/16galleries-smith-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/05/16/arts/16galleries-smith/16galleries-smith-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/05/16/arts/16galleries-smith/16galleries-smith-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1278, 'width': 1917, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/05/16/arts/16galleries-smith/16galleries-smith-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2019/05/16/arts/16galleries-smith/16galleries-smith-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/05/16/arts/16galleries-smith/16galleries-smith-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'New York Art Galleries: What to See Right Now', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Josh Smith', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Art', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Ramirez, Marcos (ERRE) (1961- )', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Smith, Josh (1976- )', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Taylor, David J (1965- )', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Tenser, Alina', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2019-05-16T14:15:37+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Weekend', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Art & Design', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/65dd6c6c-3e8b-5cd3-8b54-b6d64e3756c0', 'word_count': 890, 'uri': 'nyt://article/65dd6c6c-3e8b-5cd3-8b54-b6d64e3756c0'}, {'abstract': 'That depends on how you do the research — and then on how you read the results. Here’s what studies show.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2019/05/16/magazine/how-much-alcohol-can-you-drink-safe-health.html', 'snippet': 'That depends on how you do the research — and then on how you read the results. Here’s what studies show.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Humans have been drinking fermented concoctions since the beginning of recorded time. But despite that long relationship with alcohol, we still don’t know what exactly the molecule does to our brains to create a feeling of intoxication. Likewise, though the health harms of heavy drinking are fairly obvious, scientists have struggled to identify what negative impacts lesser volumes may lead to. Last September, the prestigious peer-reviewed British medical journal The Lancet published a study that is thought to be the most comprehensive global analysis of the risks of alcohol consumption. Its conclusion, which the media widely reported, sounded unequivocal: “The safest level of drinking is none.”', 'print_section': 'MM', 'print_page': '22', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/05/19/magazine/19Studies_01/42ae82a8ab644d10a60cc719da368d7c-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 600, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2019/05/19/magazine/19Studies_01/42ae82a8ab644d10a60cc719da368d7c-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 600}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/05/19/magazine/19Studies_01/42ae82a8ab644d10a60cc719da368d7c-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'imag