, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Taseer, Aatish', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Yuan, Jada', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'AFRICA', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Europe', 'rank': 11, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2019-05-16T16:41:48+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'TStyle', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/203c2551-b410-5251-8b74-815492a0e03e', 'word_count': 3307, 'uri': 'nyt://article/203c2551-b410-5251-8b74-815492a0e03e'}, {'abstract': 'Marilyn Stasio’s Crime column enters a dangerous online world, then jumps to a very real drug gang, a hit man in a hospital and a dog with a death sentence.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2019/05/16/books/review/new-crime-fiction-marilyn-stasio.html', 'snippet': 'Marilyn Stasio’s Crime column enters a dangerous online world, then jumps to a very real drug gang, a hit man in a hospital and a dog with a death sentence.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Got game? Jeffery Deaver creates insanely devious plots calculated to make your head explode. In THE NEVER GAME (Putnam, $28), he applies that skill to the video gaming world, with its arcane rituals, hypnotic moves and obsessive players like the geek squad that hangs out at the Quick Byte Café. This is the crowd that mobs the annual industry convention at the San Jose Exposition Center, where the visuals run to “theatrical spotlights, LEDs, backlit banners, epilepsy-inducing flashers, lasers and high-definition displays the size of school buses.”', 'print_section': 'BR', 'print_page': '9', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/05/19/books/review/19Crime/19Crime-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 707, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'l