ght': 1266, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/05/18/arts/16rolling-stones-item/16rolling-stones-item-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2019/05/18/arts/16rolling-stones-item/16rolling-stones-item-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/05/18/arts/16rolling-stones-item/16rolling-stones-item-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Rolling Stones Reschedule Tour Dates as Jagger Bounces Back From Surgery', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'The Rolling Stones To Resume Tour', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Pop and Rock Music', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Surgery and Surgeons', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Rolling Stones', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Jagger, Mick', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2019-05-16T18:29:39+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Music', 'byline': {'original': 'By Gabrielle Debinski', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Gabrielle', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Debinski', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/5461e9f8-13cb-5517-aeb7-76505bc471fe', 'word_count': 248, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5461e9f8-13cb-5517-aeb7-76505bc471fe'}, {'abstract': 'These new takes on beloved old stories deliver empowered princesses and racial diversity while staying true to the genre’s stark, dangerous heart.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2019/05/16/books/review/new-fairy-tales-rebecca-solnit.html', 'snippet': 'These new takes on beloved old stories deliver empowered princesses and racial diversity while staying true to the genre’s stark, dangerous heart.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A fairy tale, in its essence, is a story of reversal. Silent and impoverished girls discover not only voices, but jewels and riches pouring from their mouths; the castoff and abandoned find unexpected families and birthrights; mad kings and wicked stepmothers lose status, kingdoms and even lives. A fairy tale has no toleration for ambiguities. It is abrupt, immediate and often brutal — more tip of the blade than bonny glen. The dangers are real and they are everywhere. Tread carefully, these stories remind us. Keep your eyes open. Be kind and generous and fair. And for God’s sake, don’t succumb to greed, because that never ends well.', 'print_section': 'BR', 'print_page': '26', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/05/19/books/review/19Barnhill-01/19Barnhill-01-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 401, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2019/05/19/books/review/19Barnhill-01/19Barnhill-01-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 401}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/05/19/books/review/19Barnhill-01/19Barnhill-01-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 684, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/05/19/books/review/19Barnhill-01/19Barnhill-01-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1206, 'width': 1806, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtyp