'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Contests and Prizes', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Channel One', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Russia', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'The Voice Kids (TV Program)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Television', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2019-05-17T15:12:17+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Television', 'byline': {'original': 'By Sophia Kishkovsky and Alex Marshall', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Sophia', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kishkovsky', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Alex', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Marshall', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/baead556-c4e9-5744-b283-170d9eefc741', 'word_count': 527, 'uri': 'nyt://article/baead556-c4e9-5744-b283-170d9eefc741'}, {'abstract': 'Sander Lak, the creative director of Sies Marjan, shares his many inspirations with T.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2019/05/17/t-magazine/sander-lak-sies-marjan-profile-in-style.html', 'snippet': 'Sander Lak, the creative director of Sies Marjan, shares his many inspirations with T.', 'lead_paragraph': '“I’ve always felt like a bit of a nomad,” says Sander Lak, the creative director of Sies Marjan. Born in Brunei, he grew up between Malaysia, Gabon and Scotland before settling with his family in the Netherlands (his father worked as an engineer for Royal Dutch Shell). Despite being exposed to so many cultures, though, it wasn’t until high school that Lak started paying attention to clothes — and to the mid-90s indie fashions featured in Dutch magazine in particular. “I remember paging through at a gas station and thinking, ‘What is this beautiful form of storytelling?’” says Lak, 35. After getting rejected from film school, he enrolled at an arts college in Arnhem, and then at Central Saint Martins in London, which led to stints at Marc Jacobs, 3.1 Phillip Lim, Balmain and, most notably, Dries Van Noten, where he worked alongside the designer for five years. In 2015, Lak moved to New York to start his own label and became a seemingly out-of-nowhere sensation.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/05/15/t-magazine/15tmag-profile-slide-14G0/15tmag-profile-slide-14G0-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 750, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2019/05/15/t-magazine/15tmag-profile-slide-14G0/15tmag-profile-slide-14G0-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 750}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/05/15/t-magazine/15tmag-profile-slide-14G0/15tmag-profile-slide-14G0-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 819, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/05/15/t-magazine/15tmag-profile-slide-14G0/15tmag-profile-slide-14G0-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1638, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/05/15/t-magazine/15tmag-profile-slide-14G0/15tmag-profile-slide-14G0-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2019/05/15/t-magazine/15tmag-profile-slide-14G0/15tmag-profile-slide-14G0-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/05/15/t-magazine/15tmag-profile-slide-14G0/15tmag-profile-slide-14G0-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'A Designer Whose Ideal Woman Is PJ Harvey', 'kicker': 'Profile in Style', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Fashion and Apparel', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Art', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Sies Marjan (Fashion Label)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Barney, Tina', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2019-05-17T15:23:03+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'TStyle', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Lindsay Talbot', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Lindsay', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Talbot', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/830cbe2a-0c6d-571b-ba53-868efe1669f8', 'word_count': 1213, 'uri': 'nyt://article/830cbe2a-0c6d-571b-ba53-868efe1669f8'}, {'abstract': 'The countries we visited have seen years — centuries — of unimaginable wealth and power, and, equally, centuries of sorrow, despair, warfare and subjugation.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2019/05/17/t-magazine/travel-issue-letter-from-the-editor.html', 'snippet': 'The countries we visited have seen years — centuries — of unimaginable wealth and power, and, equally, centuries of sorrow, despair, warfare and subjugation.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In America, we are consumed with the idea of leisure, that pastime at which we are, as a country, particularly unskilled. Every few years, a new book is published reminding us that true contentment — or happiness, as we insist on calling it — is achievable only by doing less: less working, less texting, less consumption. Our enduring romance with Western Europe or Southern Asia may begin with its food or its art, but beneath that is our fascination with how those cultures divide their days, with their cycles of long meals and long naps.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/05/14/t-magazine/14tmag-morocco-slide-8ED2-copy/14tmag-morocco-slide-8ED2-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 450, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2019/05/14/t-magazine/14tmag-morocco-slide-8ED2-copy/14tmag-morocco-slide-8ED2-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 450}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/05/14/t-magazine/14tmag-morocco-slide-8ED2-copy/14tmag-morocco-slide-8ED2-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 768, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/05/14/t-magazine/14tmag-morocco-slide-8ED2-copy/14tmag-morocco-slide-8ED2-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1536, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/05/14/t-magazine/14tmag-morocco-slide-8ED2-copy/14tmag-morocco-slide-8ED2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2019/05/14/t-magazine/14tmag-morocco-slide-8ED2-copy/14tmag-morocco-slide-8ED2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/05/14/t-magazine/14tmag-morocco-s