e', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'C.E.O. Pay, America’s Economic ‘Miracle’', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Executive Compensation', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Corporate Taxes', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Labor and Jobs', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Stock Options and Purchase Plans', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Welch, John F Jr', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Iger, Robert A', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Disney, Abigail (1960- )', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2019-05-17T19:09:03+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Bill Saporito', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Bill', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Saporito', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/56e6365a-989e-5019-8b5f-25fbd0cefe3b', 'word_count': 1111, 'uri': 'nyt://article/56e6365a-989e-5019-8b5f-25fbd0cefe3b'}, {'abstract': 'A new mini-series demonstrates once again the difficulties of adapting Joseph Heller’s classic satire of the military mind-set.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2019/05/17/arts/television/catch-22-hulu-review.html', 'snippet': 'A new mini-series demonstrates once again the difficulties of adapting Joseph Heller’s classic satire of the military mind-set.', 'lead_paragraph': 'An attack on “Catch-22” is the kind of ultrahazardous mission for which no combat bonus could suffice. Joseph Heller’s 1961 novel toys with time, hopscotches among a huge cast of vividly defined characters and oscillates like an excited particle between Marx Brothers-level comedy and airborne battle scenes worthy of Hemingway. Adapting it for the screen is not for the fainthearted.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '7', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/05/18/arts/17catch22/merlin_154830345_6c1e6398-9931-4298-800b-f3fa4b3089d9-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2019/05/18/arts/17catch22/merlin_154830345_6c1e6398-9931-4298-800b-f3fa4b3089d9-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/05/18/arts/17catch22/merlin_154830345_6c1e6398-9931-4298-800b-f3fa4b3089d9-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/05/18/arts/17catch22/merlin_154830345_6c1e6398-9931-4298-800b-f3fa4b3089d9-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/05/18/arts/17catch22/merlin_154830345_6c1e6398-9931-4298-800b-f3fa4b3089d9-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2019/05/18/arts/17catch22/merlin_154830345_6c1e6398-9931-4298-800b-f3fa4b3089d9-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/05/18/arts/17catch22/merlin_154830345_6c1e6398-9931-4298-800b-f3fa4b3089d9-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Review: From George Clooney and Hulu, ‘Catch-22,’ With a Catch', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Major Major Novel on the Small Small Screen', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Television', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Hulu.com', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'Catch-22 (TV Program)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'CATCH-22 (BOOK)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2019-05-17T19:14:53+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Television', 'byline': {'original': 'By Mike Hale', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Mike', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Hale', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/2cf2a2cd-13d1-5fff-99a8-879b2d11a9b9', 'word_count': 841, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2cf2a2cd-13d1-5fff-99a8-879b2d11a9b9'}, {'abstract': 'The CBS comedy will finish the season as the most-viewed entertainment show in all of network television.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2019/05/17/arts/television/big-bang-theory-ratings.html', 'snippet': 'The CBS comedy will finish the season as the most-viewed entertainment show in all of network television.', 'lead_paragraph': '“The Big Bang Theory” ended its long, successful run with 18 million people tuning in for its series finale on Thursday night, according to Nielsen.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/08/23/business/17bang-ratings/17bang-ratings-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 573, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2018/08/23/business/17bang-ratings