'_id': 'nyt://article/1846d4ef-b2cf-5b6a-affd-4f8bd5dd87af', 'word_count': 885, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1846d4ef-b2cf-5b6a-affd-4f8bd5dd87af'}, {'abstract': 'He was never all that lovable a figure, and he is hardly an exemplar of fine behavior off the course, but fans love golf’s past and current king.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2019/05/17/sports/pga-tiger-golf.html', 'snippet': 'He was never all that lovable a figure, and he is hardly an exemplar of fine behavior off the course, but fans love golf’s past and current king.', 'lead_paragraph': 'FARMINGDALE, N.Y. — The crowds following Tiger Woods on the Black Course at Bethpage State Park this week looked more like a marauding army than a gathering of golf fans on a pleasant day. They trampled everything in their path and went under and over ropes designed to prevent them from doing exactly that. One fan even broke a fence trying to get a better view of Woods over the swarming masses.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '7', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/05/17/sports/17tigerfans/merlin_154872294_04704cd3-95f3-4eff-ae6f-64d4434859c7-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 1293, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2019/05/17/sports/17tigerfans/merlin_154872294_04704cd3-95f3-4eff-ae6f-64d4434859c7-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 1293}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/05/17/sports/17tigerfans/merlin_154872294_04704cd3-95f3-4eff-ae6f-64d4434859c7-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 476, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/05/17/sports/17tigerfans/merlin_154872294_04704cd3-95f3-4eff-ae6f-64d4434859c7-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 204