one}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/0ee8e346-6202-5878-9ed8-4d70c52b97c6', 'word_count': 1008, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0ee8e346-6202-5878-9ed8-4d70c52b97c6'}, {'abstract': 'A film exposing sex abuse by Catholic priests also exposes the corrupting ties between the church and the ruling political party.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2019/05/18/opinion/poland-church-abuse.html', 'snippet': 'A film exposing sex abuse by Catholic priests also exposes the corrupting ties between the church and the ruling political party.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Following sexual-abuse scandals in the United States, Britain, Ireland and Australia, it seems that the Roman Catholic Church may be on the verge of a similar catastrophe in Poland. But whereas the blowback from previous scandals has been largely confined to the church itself, this latest crisis could take down the country’s right-wing government as well — and undermine the tight grip the church holds over Polish society. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/05/20/opinion/18SierakWeb/db2ae760a8d5497faff8ba13c06f6c0b-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 399, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2019/05/20/opinion/18SierakWeb/db2ae760a8d5497faff8ba13c06f6c0b-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 399}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/05/20/opinion/18SierakWeb/db2ae760a8d5497faff8ba13c06f6c0b-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 682, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/05/20/opinion/18SierakWeb/db2ae760a8d5497faff8ba13c06f6c0b-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1363, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}},