7, 'uri': 'nyt://article/bc5cfd99-02ce-50e3-aac1-81d302f136aa'}, {'abstract': 'Warmer weather brings daffodils, rhubarb at the farmer’s market — and, for some, despair.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2019/05/18/opinion/sunday/spring-despair.html', 'snippet': 'Warmer weather brings daffodils, rhubarb at the farmer’s market — and, for some, despair.', 'lead_paragraph': 'It’s a popular and perhaps dangerous belief, reinforced by that inescapable Christmas classic “It’s a Wonderful Life,” that winter is the peak season for suicide. Yet experts have known since the late 1800s that it’s not true: More people take their own lives in the spring months than in other times of the year. No definitive explanations have emerged for why this is so.', 'print_section': 'SR', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/05/19/opinion/sunday/19Cregan/e521346f27f74c52a69aaf81ef9afe31-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 421, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2019/05/19/opinion/sunday/19Cregan/e521346f27f74c52a69aaf81ef9afe31-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 421}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/05/19/opinion/sunday/19Cregan/e521346f27f74c52a69aaf81ef9afe31-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 719, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/05/19/opinion/sunday/19Cregan/e521346f27f74c52a69aaf81ef9afe31-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1437, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/05/19/opinion/sunday/19Cregan/19Cregan-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2019/05/19/opinion/sunday/19Cregan/19Cregan-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/05/19/opinion/sunday/19Cregan/19Cregan-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': '‘I Had Completely Lost the Knack for Staying Alive’', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Spring Can Be a Sad Season', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Spring (Season)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Depression (Mental)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Mental Health and Disorders', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Suicides and Suicide Attempts', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2019-05-18T18:30:07+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'subsection_name': 'Sunday Review', 'byline': {'original': 'By Mary Cregan', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Mary', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Cregan', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/fdadd3c6-f678-50c4-8eb5-bd30c91f29d3', 'word_count': 1134, 'uri': 'nyt://article/fdadd3c6-f678-50c4-8eb5-bd30c91f29d3'}, {'abstract': 'How a war in the Middle East would wreck Trump’s grand strategy.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2019/05/18/opinion/sunday/trump-iran-war.html', 'snippet': 'How a war in the Middle East would wreck Trump’s grand strategy.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Sometimes it’s important to write a column about something you’re pretty sure isn’t going to happen. In this case, that thing is war with Iran, which Donald Trump clearly doesn’t