8b32-78df5dd4971f'}, {'abstract': 'Ms. Harris would force companies with 100 or more employees to show they were paying men and women equally for analogous work, penalizing those that didn’t.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2019/05/20/us/politics/kamala-harris-gender-pay-gap.html', 'snippet': 'Ms. Harris would force companies with 100 or more employees to show they were paying men and women equally for analogous work, penalizing those that didn’t.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Senator Kamala Harris of California on Monday announced a proposal to close the gender wage gap by requiring larger companies to certify that men and women are paid equally, in an effort to combat wage discrimination on a federal level.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '14', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Kamala Harris Announces Plan to Close the Gender Pay Gap', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Harris Offers Plan to Close Gap in Pay For Women', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Wages and Salaries', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Presidential Election of 2020', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Harris, Kamala D', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Discrimination', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Women and Girls', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Income Inequality', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2019-05-20T10:00:05+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Politics', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Astead W. Herndon', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Astead', 'middlename': 'W.', 'lastname': 'Herndon', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f62d2768-70a4-5461-a4ae-0758fda75f67', 'word_count': 531, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f62d2768-70a4-5461-a4ae-0758fda75f67'}, {'abstract': 'I’m tempted to say there’s never been a worse time to be a sentient human being below the Mason-Dixon line, but I know that’s not true.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2019/05/20/opinion/the-american-south.html', 'snippet': 'I’m tempted to say there’s never been a worse time to be a sentient human being below the Mason-Dixon line, but I know that’s not true.', 'lead_paragraph': 'NASHVILLE — The news emanating from the American South this year has been one long litany of assaults against human decency. In Alabama, a physician who performs an abortion in the case of rape may soon spend more time in prison than the rapist himself. In Mississippi, a family is suing the county and its sheriff for beating a black man to death in jail. Tennessee just executed a deeply repentant Christian convert who had lived an exemplary life in prison. Proponents of a “culture of life” don’t seem to recognize the incoherence of their position. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/05/20/opinion/20renkl1/merlin_153218049_89ed0c6b-372a-4c14-aa60-79f5daf5cfa0-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2019/05/20/opinion/20renkl1/merlin_153218049_89ed0c6b-372a-4c14-aa60-79f5daf5cfa0-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/05/20/opinion/20renkl1/merlin_153218049_89ed0c6b-372a-4c14-aa60-79f5daf5cfa0-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/05/20/opinion/20renkl1/merlin_153218049_89ed0c6b-372a-4c14-aa60-79f5daf5cfa0-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/05/20/opinion/20renkl1/20renkl1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2019/05/20/opinion/20renkl1/20renkl1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/05/20/opinion/20renkl1/20renkl1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Shame and Salvation in the American South', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Southern States (US)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'ABORTION', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Politics and Government', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Blacks', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Black People', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Race and Ethnicity', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'ALABAMA', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2019-05-20T10:00:06+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Margaret Renkl', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Margaret', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Renkl', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/d50a7406-cafd-5c80-87ef-baef9b2c3858', 'word_count': 1046, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d50a7406-cafd-5c80-87ef-baef9b2c3858'}, {'abstract': 'Congress needs the full report to do its job.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2019/05/20/opinion/trump-mueller-report.html', 'snippet': 'Congress needs the full report to do its job.', 'lead_paragraph': 'You may have a hard time believing a key argument the Trump administration is using to rebuff efforts by Congress to obtain information legislators need to do their job. The administration has claimed — for example, in a letter from the White House counsel to the House Judiciary Committee in response to congressional subpoenas of the full Mueller report — that Congress must demonstrate to the administration’s satisfaction that the information would serve a “legitimate legislative purpose.” In effect, Congress must show that its interests fall within the power under Article I of the Constitution to pass new legislation.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/05/20/opinion/20goodman1web/merlin_153697296_67d2bb77-49f0-4aea-af53-d6e0d8cba022-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2019/05/20/opinion/20goodman1web/merlin_153697296_67d2bb77-49f0-4aea-af53-d6e0d8cba022-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/05/20/opinion/20goodman1web/merlin_153697296_67d2bb77-49f0-4aea-af53-d6e0d8cba022-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/05/20/opinion/20goodman1web/merlin_153697296_67d2bb77-49f0-4aea-af53-d6e0d8cba022-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/05/20/opinion/20goodman1web/20goodman1web-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2019/05/20/opinion/20goodman1web/20goodman1web-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/05/20/opinion/20goodman1web/20goodman1web-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Trump’s Position on the Mueller Report is Legally Ridiculous — and Dangerous', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Politics and Government', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Russian Interference in 2016 US Elections and Ties to Trump Associates', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Law and Legislation', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Constitution (US)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Campaign Finance', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Federal Election Commission', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Mueller, Robert S III', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'House Committee on the Judiciary', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'House of Representatives', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Justice Department', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Supreme Court (US)', 'rank': 11, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Mehta, Amit P', 'rank': 12, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Trump, Donald J', 'rank': 13, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2019-05-20T10:00:06+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ryan Goodman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ryan', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Goodman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/fab5674a-f21f-5298-a643-37deea6f0efa', 'word_count': 863, 'uri': 'nyt://article/fab5674a-f21f-5298-a643-37deea6f0efa'}, {'abstract': 'Vehicles collect a lot of unusual data. But who owns it?', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2019/05/20/opinion/car-repair-data-privacy.html', 'snippet': 'Vehicles collect a lot of unusual data. But who owns it?', 'lead_paragraph': 'Cars produced today are essentially smartphones with wheels. For drivers, this has meant many new features: automatic braking, turn-by-turn directions, infotainment. But for all the things we’re getting out of our connected vehicles, carmakers are getting much, much more: They’re constantly collecting data from our vehicles.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/05/22/opinion/sunday/17Hanvey/3c27e820db0d4c6aa06dd2df1d9c33dc-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 600, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2019/05/22/opinion/sunday/17Hanvey/3c27e820db0d4c6aa06dd2df1d9c33dc-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 600}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/05/22/opinion/sunday/17Hanvey/3c27e820db0d4c6aa06dd2df1d9c33dc-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/05/22/opinion/sunday/17Hanvey/3c27e820db0d4c6aa06dd2df1d9c33dc-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 