eractive/bd6d2f5c-1ad2-52fa-92ea-29d08e01d55e'}, {'abstract': 'Pay attention to your environment. Wear indistinct clothing. Consider a “heat run.”', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2019/05/21/magazine/how-to-lose-a-tail-tip.html', 'snippet': 'Pay attention to your environment. Wear indistinct clothing. Consider a “heat run.”', 'lead_paragraph': '“Keep your eyes open and your head swiveling around,” says Scott Wright, a former special agent for the United States Secret Service who protected numerous heads of state during his career, including George H.W. Bush, the Clintons and Gerald Ford. He now instructs criminal investigators at the Federal Law Enforcement Training Center in Glynco, Ga. “Try to remember the faces and cars you see,” Wright says. Notice who and what is in your environment so that you have a baseline and can spot when something is awry. The sooner you’re clued in to a follower, the more options you have to evade them.', 'print_section': 'MM', 'print_page': '19', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/05/26/magazine/26Mag-Tip-1/26Mag-Tip-1-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 470, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2019/05/26/magazine/26Mag-Tip-1/26Mag-Tip-1-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 470}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/05/26/magazine/26Mag-Tip-1/26Mag-Tip-1-jumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 801, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/05/26/magazine/26Mag-Tip-1/26Mag-Tip-1-superJumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 1447, 'width': 1849, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None,