tname': 'Cappelle', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/f077b2bb-0206-5894-ba20-a176572e33c8', 'word_count': 1084, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f077b2bb-0206-5894-ba20-a176572e33c8'}, {'abstract': 'Power is acting for good — and knowing when you should.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2019/05/23/opinion/power-moral-courage.html', 'snippet': 'Power is acting for good — and knowing when you should.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Over the years, thousands of cadets at the United States Military Academy, myself included, have memorized and recited West Point’s Cadet Prayer. “Make us to choose the harder right instead of the easier wrong,” the prayer goes, “and never to be content with a half-truth when the whole can be won. Endow us with courage that is born of loyalty to all that is noble and worthy, that scorns to compromise with vice and injustice, and knows no fear when truth and right are in jeopardy.”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/05/25/opinion/25powerclark1/merlin_154955856_51b9b13d-272a-418a-9fab-d2c60cb10500-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2019/05/25/opinion/25powerclark1/merlin_154955856_51b9b13d-272a-418a-9fab-d2c60cb10500-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/05/25/opinion/25powerclark1/merlin_154955856_51b9b13d-272a-418a-9fab-d2c60cb10500-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/05/25/opinion/25powerclark1/merlin_154955856_51b9b13d-272a-418a-9fab-d2c60cb10500-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/05/25/opinion/25powerclark1/25powerclark1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2019/05/25/opinion/25powerclark1/25powerclark1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/05/25/opinion/25powerclark1/25powerclark1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'What Happens When Our Leaders Lack Moral Courage', 'kicker': 'THE big ideas: what is power?', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'War Crimes, Genocide and Crimes Against Humanity', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Defense and Military Forces', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Ethics (Personal)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Philosophy', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2019-05-23T10:00:04+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Wesley K. Clark', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Wesley', 'middlename': 'K.', 'lastname': 'Clark', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/b4171bf1-eaee-50cf-b184-339b3ee78f8b', 'word_count': 1179, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b4171bf1-eaee-50cf-b184-339b3ee78f8b'}, {'abstract': 'The theocratic regime could not long survive if the Islamic republic acted like most nations.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2019/05/23/opinion/iran-trump.html', 'snippet': 'The theocratic regime could not long survive if the Islamic republic acted like most nations.', 'lead_paragraph': 'There has always been a fair and symmetrical formula for the United States and Iran to resolve the full range of their differences: full normalization for full normalization. Donald Trump, who may — but probably doesn’t — want a war with the Islamic republic, should propose it, publicly and in detail, and see what happens. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/05/24/opinion/22stepehensWeb/merlin_155102409_9aecb3f1-35cd-4108-bd6c-e68101493287-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 396, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2019/05/24/opinion/22stepehensWeb/merlin_155102409_9aecb3f1-35cd-4108-bd6c-e68101493287-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 396}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/05/24/opinion/22stepehensWeb/merlin_155102409_9aecb3f1-35cd-4108-bd6c-e68101493287-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 676, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/05/24/opinion/22stepehensWeb/merlin_155102409_9aecb3f1-35cd-4108-bd6c-e68101493287-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1352, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/05/24/opinion/22stepehensWeb/22stepehensWeb-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2019/05/24/opinion/22stepehensWeb/22stepehensWeb-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheig