ount': 252, 'uri': 'nyt://article/338cb097-f513-5229-b44c-b4ece17f7c19'}, {'abstract': 'Household finances are improving in a strong job market, but just six in 10 adults still could cover a surprise expense without selling something or borrowing money.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2019/05/23/business/economy/fed-400-dollar-survey.html', 'snippet': 'Household finances are improving in a strong job market, but just six in 10 adults still could cover a surprise expense without selling something or borrowing money.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Four in 10 American adults wouldn’t be able to cover an unexpected $400 expense with cash, savings or a credit-card charge that could be quickly paid off, a new Federal Reserve survey finds.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/05/24/business/24DC-FEDSURVEY-01-print/24DC-FEDSURVEY-01-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 413, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2019/05/24/business/24DC-FEDSURVEY-01-print/24DC-FEDSURVEY-01-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 413}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/05/24/business/24DC-FEDSURVEY-01-print/24DC-FEDSURVEY-01-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 704, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/05/24/business/24DC-FEDSURVEY-01-print/24DC-FEDSURVEY-01-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1408, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/05/24/business/24DC-FEDSURVEY-01-print/24DC-FEDSURVEY-01-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2019/05/24/business/24DC-FEDSURVEY-01-print/24DC-FEDSURVEY-01-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/05/24/business/24DC-FEDSURVEY-01-print/24DC-FEDSURVEY-01-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Many Adults Would Struggle to Find $400, the Fed Finds', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Many American Adults Live On Financial Edge, Fed Says', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Economy', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Labor and Jobs', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Federal Reserve System', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Personal Finances', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Wages and Salaries', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Savings', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Credit and Debt', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2019-05-23T16:01:26+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Economy', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jeanna Smialek', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jeanna', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Smialek', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/9c0b3228-c00b-57ca-840e-4f49649b1c0d', 'word_count': 406, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9c0b3228-c00b-57ca-840e-4f49649b1c0d'}, {'abstract': 'In New York, the chef and artist Laila Gohar hosted an evening inspired by an Egyptian holiday.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2019/05/23/t-magazine/laila-gohar-dinner-party.html', 'snippet': 'In New York, the chef and artist Laila Gohar hosted an evening inspired by an Egyptian holiday.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The chef and artist Laila Gohar moved to New York City 10 years ago, but it was only recently that she began to feel a longing for home. Gohar was born and raised in Cairo — where winters are mild, and summers come hot and quick — and makes a living creating interactive installations at fashion and art events (imagine, for example, cracking open a salt-baked pear with a wooden mallet at the recent Object & Thing design fair). Though she and her husband, Omar Sosa, one of the Barcelona-born co-founders of Apartamento magazine, have made a home for themselves in a cozy third-floor apartment on Spring Street in Manhattan, Gohar admits she still feels “very much like a foreigner” in the United States. Which is why, on a recent evening, she assembled some of her closest friends — including the fashion designer Maryam Nassir Zadeh, the actor and director Hailey Gates and the creative director Rafael Prieto — for dinner to celebrate an Egyptian holiday called Sham el-Nessim. The tradition, which means “smelling the breeze” in Arabic, is believed to be as old as the pharaohs, and celebrates the arrival of spring. Egyptians gather outdoors in public gardens, in zoos, in public spaces, on boats on the Nile and elsewhere, and feast on salted fermented fish, lettuce, beans and boiled eggs — all foods believed to be what was originally offered to the gods in ancient times. “In Cairo, it’s a really fun day,” explained Gohar. “There are people from all walks of life — it’s not a religious holiday — young and old, rich and poor, everyone celebrates the holiday.”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/05/14/t-magazine/14tmag-laila-11/823c3c1d818d43498f6ceef0dc44b986-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2019/05/14/t-magazine/14tmag-laila-11/823c3c1d818d43498f6ceef0dc44b986-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/05/14/t-magazine/14tmag-laila-11/823c3c1d818d43498f6ceef0dc44b986-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/05/14/t-magazine/14tmag-laila-11/823c3c1d818d43498f6ceef0dc44b986-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/05/14/t-magazine/14tmag-laila-11/14tmag-laila-11-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2019/05/14/t-magazine/14tmag-laila-11/14tmag-laila-11-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/05/14/t-magazine/14tmag-laila-11/14tmag-laila-11-thumbLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'How to Throw a Celebratory Spring Dinner Party', 'kicker': 'Entertaining With', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cooking and Cookbooks', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Desserts', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Egyptian-Americans', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Parties (Social)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'She Wolf (Brooklyn, NY, Bakery)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Zadeh, Maryam Nassir', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Mattos, Ignacio', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York City', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2019-05-23T16:04:59+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'TStyle', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Thessaly La Force', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Thessaly', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'La Force', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/34ad9072-1d3d-53bb-992b-ecef8661c65d', 'word_count': 1366, 'uri': 'nyt://article/34ad9072-1d3d-53bb-992b-ecef8661c65d'}, {'abstract': 'How fast you react to warnings and where you take shelter can make all the difference when a tornado strikes. Here is what experts say will keep you safest.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2019/05/23/us/tornado-safety-tips-jefferson-city-missouri.html', 'snippet': 'How fast you react to warnings and where you take shelter can make all the difference when a tornado strikes. Here is what experts say will keep you safest.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Strong storms sweeping across the Plains and Midwest over the past two weeks have spawned a wave of destructive tornadoes, including a cluster that touched down in Kansas and Missouri Tuesday evening and at least 10 in Ohio the previous night, wrecking houses and causing at least one death.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/05/23/us/23tornado-tips/merlin_155199579_5e1e6561-7cad-414b-b8f7-185210f1e46b-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 399, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2019/05/23/us/23tornado-tips/merlin_155199579_5e1e6561-7cad-414b-b8f7-185210f1e46b-arti