s the Japanese novel that begot it.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2019/05/23/arts/design/genji-met-museum-review.html', 'snippet': 'A show at the Metropolitan Museum is as sumptuous and seductive as the Japanese novel that begot it.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Not every enduring literary masterpiece inspires a thousand years of often great art. “The Tale of Genji,” written in early-11th-century Japan and possibly the world’s first novel, is an exception. A narratively rich saga of life and love at the Japanese imperial court, it spurred innovation and was in many ways foundational to Japanese art itself. ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '19', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/05/23/arts/23talesofgenji1/merlin_155246337_365b8561-0e2d-446f-b17e-2b7d9c1195dd-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 691, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2019/05/23/arts/23talesofgenji1/merlin_155246337_365b8561-0e2d-446f-b17e-2b7d9c1195dd-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 691}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/05/23/arts/23talesofgenji1/merlin_155246337_365b8561-0e2d-446f-b17e-2b7d9c1195dd-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 890, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/05/23/arts/23talesofgenji1/merlin_155246337_365b8561-0e2d-446f-b17e-2b7d9c1195dd-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1779, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/05/23/arts/23talesofgenji1/23talesofgenji1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', '