 {'main': 'A Lesson for (and From) a Dystopian World', 'kicker': 'THE big ideas: what is power?', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Lesson for a Dystopian World', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Language and Languages', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Philosophy', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2019-05-26T23:00:07+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Rowan Williams', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Rowan', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Williams', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/ff2ab30e-c777-5c38-9845-a0ae33dba267', 'word_count': 1006, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ff2ab30e-c777-5c38-9845-a0ae33dba267'}, {'abstract': 'The Supreme Court’s legal abuse of Native Americans set the stage for America’s poor treatment of many of its vulnerable populations.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2019/05/26/opinion/american-indian-law-trump.html', 'snippet': 'The Supreme Court’s legal abuse of Native Americans set the stage for America’s poor treatment of many of its vulnerable populations.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The first two years of the Trump administration have brought us horror story after horror story about our government: children separated from their families, men and women detained without due process, communities punished because of their faith. These horrors may seem new, but in fact these abuses — and in particular the law that authorizes them — have been part of our constitutional order since the founding of this country.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '19', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'image