ntles patriarchal social structures and allows us to rebuild them with equity at their foundation.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2019/05/28/opinion/women-anarchy-patriarchy.html', 'snippet': 'Power is anarchy. It dismantles patriarchal social structures and allows us to rebuild them with equity at their foundation.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Like a lot of Black women, I have always had to invent the power my freedom requires. — June Jordan, “On Call: Political Essays” (1985)', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/05/30/opinion/28powerSub/merlin_154836576_3c65be31-72fe-4bef-9a1d-5946cd20e24c-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2019/05/30/opinion/28powerSub/merlin_154836576_3c65be31-72fe-4bef-9a1d-5946cd20e24c-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/05/30/opinion/28powerSub/merlin_154836576_3c65be31-72fe-4bef-9a1d-5946cd20e24c-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/05/30/opinion/28powerSub/merlin_154836576_3c65be31-72fe-4bef-9a1d-5946cd20e24c-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/05/30/opinion/28powerSub/28powerSub-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2019/05/30/opinion/28powerSub/28powerSub-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/05/30/opinion/28powerSub/28powerSub-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Enough With Crumbs — I Want the Cake', 'kicker': 'THE big ideas: What is Power?', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Women and Girls', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'World Cup 2018 (Soccer)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Philosophy', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Brazil', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2019-05-28T10:00:06+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Mona Eltahawy', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Mona', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Eltahawy', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/67451857-78c6-5d80-9b08-d64c87a494e6', 'word_count': 1409, 'uri': 'nyt://article/67451857-78c6-5d80-9b08-d64c87a494e6'}, {'abstract': 'Since the fall of the Berlin Wall, a series of discriminatory labor practices have emerged that threaten the inclusion of Afro-Cubans in the island’s new economic reality.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2019/05/28/opinion/cuban-revolution-racism.html', 'snippet': 'Since the fall of the Berlin Wall, a series of discriminatory labor practices have emerged that threaten the inclusion of Afro-Cubans in the island’s new economic reality.', 'lead_paragraph': 'CAMBRIDGE, Mass. — A common scene plays out in Havana: four female Spanish tourists arrive at one of the city’s many nightclubs in the company of two Afro-Cuban men. “You’re in, but they’re not,” the bouncer tells them. “The house reserves the right of admission.” The tourists protest, citing such practices as those of “a racist country,” but in the end their companions are denied entry. They’ll have to try their luck elsewhere. Cuba’s social policies benefited most of the population, regardless of color, but it’s clear they did not succeed in putting an end to racism. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/05/28/opinion/28delafuente-1/merlin_136233003_658a1518-cf71-4800-bbd4-3a26efea329e-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2019/05/28/opinion/28delafuente-1/merlin_136233003_658a1518-cf71-4800-bbd4-3a26efea329e-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/05/28/opinion/28delafuente-1/merlin_136233003_658a1518-cf71-4800-bbd4-3a26efea329e-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/05/28/opinion/28delafuente-1/merlin_136233003_658a1518-cf71-4800-bbd4-3a26efea329e-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/05/28/opinion/28delafuente-1/28delafuente-1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2019/05/28/opinion/28delafuente-1/28delafuente-1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/05/28/opinion/28delafuente-1/28delafuente-1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge',