re on Santorini, or to garnish baked fish. Jammy spoon sweets come in offbeat flavors like bergamot and sour cherry. The cherry, in particular, is a nice addition to your old-fashioned.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/05/29/dining/27burner3/27burner3-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 419, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2019/05/29/dining/27burner3/27burner3-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 419}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/05/29/dining/27burner3/27burner3-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 714, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/05/29/dining/27burner3/27burner3-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1429, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/05/29/dining/27burner3/27burner3-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2019/05/29/dining/27burner3/27burner3-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/05/29/dining/27burner3/27burner3-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Greek Goods for Your Pantry', 'kicker': 'Front Burner', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'To Shop: Greek Goods For Your Pantry', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cooking and Cookbooks', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'E-Commerce', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Greek Food (Cuisine)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Kochilas, Diane', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2019-05-28T17:24:09+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Dining', 'section_name': 'Food', 'byline': {'original': 'By Florence Fabricant', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Florence', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Fabricant', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f3b58bc4-af4c-52f5-a14a-d9a649f5546b', 'word_count': 145, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f3b58bc4-af4c-52f5-a14a-d9a649f5546b'}, {'abstract': 'A barrel of Champagne. At least that is what this winemaker is banking on you to do.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2019/05/28/dining/drinks/champagne-paul-launois.html', 'snippet': 'A barrel of Champagne. At least that is what this winemaker is banking on you to do.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Champagne is based on tradition, but Champagne Paul Launois is going its own way. And those with some spare change can wind up with 216 bottles labeled with their names and made according to their tastes. Julien and Sarah Launois, who started the small estate in Le Mesnil-sur-Oger in 2015, produce 20 barrels of softly elegant and innovative single-barrel grand cru blanc de blancs Champagne each year, some of which are sold to a closed group of collectors. This year, they’re also offering 10 of them to the public at an auction on June 14. Details like the finish for the oak, the amount of aging on the lees and the addition of the final dosage, or sweetness added while bottling, can vary from barrel to barrel. During the aging process, from three to 10 years, the buyers can visit their barrels, pet them, whisper encouragement and sample the wine. At the live and phone auction, the minimum price per barrel will be 23,400 euros, or about $26,000, which works out to about $120 a bottle.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/05/29/dining/29Burner-Champagne/merlin_155509665_33655712-e29d-46de-9770-0bdbe29f0467-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 2130, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2019/05/29/dining/29Burner-Champagne/merlin_155509665_33655712-e29d-46de-9770-0bdbe29f0467-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 2130}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/05/29/dining/29Burner-Champagne/merlin_155509665_33655712-e29d-46de-9770-0bdbe29f0467-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 289, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/05/29/dining/29Burner-Champagne/merlin_155509665_33655712-e29d-46de-9770-0bdbe29f0467-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 577, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/05/29/dining/29Burner-Champagne/29Burner-Champagne-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2019/05/29/dining/29Burner-Champagne/29Burner-Champagne-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/05/29/dining/29Burner-Champagne/29Burner-Champagne-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'What Do You Give Someone With Everything?', 'kicker': 'Front Burner', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'To Commission: Rolling Out Champagne. In a Barrel, of Course.', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Champagne (Wine)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Auctions', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Champagne Paul Launois', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Champagne Region (France)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2019-05-28T17:28:35+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Dining', 'section_name': 'Food', 'subsection_name': 'Wine, Beer & Cocktails', 'byline': {'original': 'By Florence Fabricant', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Florence', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Fabricant', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f2eba7a9-3948-521e-8ee1-206aa197b124', 'word_count': 210, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f2eba7a9-3948-521e-8ee1-206aa197b124'}, {'abstract': 'BonBon on the Lower East Side now offers soft serve in addition to its gummy delights.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2019/05/28/dining/bonbon-swedish-candy-soft-serve.html', 'snippet': 'BonBon on the Lower East Side now offers soft serve in addition to its gummy delights.', 'lead_paragraph': 'BonBon, a candy store that sells imported Swedish confections by the pound, has added soft-serve ice cream. There’s an exceptionally creamy chocolate and a vegan vanilla, made with coconut oil and water, which has a slightly icy sorbet consistency. That one rotates in for regular vanilla on various days. The soft serve is not from Sweden, but the toppings are. They include licorice, raspberry-licorice fudge and tutti-frutti. Sauces like green apple and salty licorice can be drizzled on top. The shop also sells a thin plastic glove to protect the eater from drips.', 'print_section': 'D', 'p