t_headline': 'To Lap: Swedish Candy Shop  Adds Frozen Treats', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'BonBon NYC (Manhattan, NY, Retailer)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Ice Cream and Frozen Desserts', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Candy', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Lower East Side (Manhattan, NY)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2019-05-28T17:35:11+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Dining', 'section_name': 'Food', 'byline': {'original': 'By Florence Fabricant', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Florence', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Fabricant', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c68469b4-3d49-5d7a-a4e1-6679386573f6', 'word_count': 135, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c68469b4-3d49-5d7a-a4e1-6679386573f6'}, {'abstract': 'A new design book looks at 20th-century kitchens, from appliance to paint.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2019/05/28/dining/midcentury-kitchen-book.html', 'snippet': 'A new design book looks at 20th-century kitchens, from appliance to paint.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The post-World War II evolution of the American kitchen was not simply a matter of design and technology. As the design writer Sarah Archer explains, it was largely driven by social changes, especially concerning the role of women. Ms. Archer starts with the history of the kitchen and then covers the evolution of its features, including the standardization of dimensions and of appliances, advances like freezing and tastes in color — avocado and even bright red, for everything. And though a sleek space-age look was heavily promoted at World’s Fairs and even in Moscow at the exhibition that led to  the confrontation between Richard M. Nixon, then the vice president, and Nikita Khrushchev, it appears that vintage charm still has its champions.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/05/29/dining/27burner1/27burner1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 743, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2019/05/29/dining/27burner1/27burner1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 743}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/05/29/dining/27burner1/27burner1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 828, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/05/29/dining/27burner1/27burner1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1655, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/05/29/dining/27burner1/27burner1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2019/05/29/dining/27burner1/27burner1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/05/29/dining/27burner1/27burner1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'A Refreshing Retro-Kitchen History', 'kicker': 'Front Burner', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'To Survey: A Refreshing  Retro-Kitchen History', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Kitchens', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Design', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': "The