pete to be the next Watermelon Thump Queen.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2019/05/28/opinion/watermelon-pageant.html', 'snippet': 'In Luling, the “toughest town in Texas,” two Latina high school girls compete to be the next Watermelon Thump Queen.', 'lead_paragraph': 'We ended up in Luling, Tex. (pop. 5,700), in search of great barbecue. While the legendary City Market didn’t disappoint, our post-meal stroll through the quiet streets of what calls itself the “toughest town in Texas,” lit by the harshly beautiful Texas sunset, led us to far more than just the perfect smoked sausage. Everywhere we turned, we spied handmade, glitter-encrusted signs encouraging passers-by to vote for one young woman or another to be the next Watermelon Thump Queen. They were hung on shop windows and long-abandoned buildings, stapled to wooden stakes driven into front yards, even plastered on the enclosures surrounding the rusting, intermittently gyrating jack pumps that dot Luling’s landscape, a reminder of the town’s history as the center of one of the first Texas oil booms.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Vying for the Watermelon Thump Crown', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Beauty Contests', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Luling (Tex)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hispanic-Americans', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Teenagers and Adolescence', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Women and Girls', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Elections', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2019-05-28T19:08:45+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Farihah Zaman and Jeff Reichert', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Farihah', 'middlename': None, 'lastn