None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Tennis', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'French Open (Tennis)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Chile', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Garin, Cristian', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2019-05-28T21:00:39+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ben Rothenberg', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ben', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Rothenberg', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/caa6cbae-d087-5791-96af-65ecebd7237a', 'word_count': 992, 'uri': 'nyt://article/caa6cbae-d087-5791-96af-65ecebd7237a'}, {'abstract': 'Whether you’re looking for princes, priestesses, or competent women running the show, there’s a book for you this summer.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2019/05/28/books/review/summer-romance-novels-alyssa-cole-alisha-rai-casey-mcquiston-maxym-martineau.html', 'snippet': 'Whether you’re looking for princes, priestesses, or competent women running the show, there’s a book for you this summer.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The fantasy of a romance novel isn’t always in the love story. Some of the most powerful escapism comes from setting real, flawed characters in fantastical worlds. Whether the departures from our grubby reality are minor or profound, these imaginary worlds offer hopeful possibilities — for love to flourish, for injustice to be righted, for beauty to persevere. Or sometimes they’re just a lovely place to spend a few hours while you read. Just as fantastical as a magical realm of otherworldly beasts and shadow-dwelling assassins is an alternate-timeline America where the president is a brilliant woman and the hottest tabloid fodder is a true and charming love. Whether you want modern-day royalty, supernatural powers or just supernaturally competent women running the show, here are four new romances that will sweep you away.', 'print_section': 'BR', 'print_page': '29', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/06/02/books/review/02Romance-GREEN/merlin_155159316_ea7a70fb-628f-4612-a006-e56d8fccba2d-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 719, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2019/06/02/books/review/02Romance-GREEN/merlin_155159316_ea7a70fb-628f-4612-a006-e56d8fccba2d-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 719}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/06/02/books/review/02Romance-GREEN/merlin_155159316_ea7a70fb-628f-4612-a006-e56d8fccba2d-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 855, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/06/02/books/review/02Romance-GREEN/merlin_155159316_ea7a70fb-628f-4612-a006-e56d8fccba2d-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1656, 'width': 1382, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/06/02/books/review/02Romance-GREEN/02Romance-GREEN-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2019/06/02/books/review/02Romance-GREEN/02Romance-GREEN-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/06/02/books/review/02Romance-GREEN/02Romance-GREEN-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Four Delicious New Romance No