.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2019/05/30/movies/echo-in-the-canyon-review.html', 'snippet': 'Stars from bands of the 1960s and beyond share their memories of a time and place that made lasting changes in popular music.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The delight of “Echo in the Canyon” is in the delicious details its subjects impart. Michelle Phillips of the Mamas and the Papas remembers Brian Wilson’s living room, a piano planted on the sand-covered floor as he wrote the Beach Boys’ influential “Pet Sounds” album; Tom Petty notes that “Pet Sounds” was considered to be responsible for “Sgt. Pepper”; a white-maned David Crosby reveals why he was ejected from the Byrds; and the narrator, the singer-songwriter Jakob Dylan, coaxes Stephen Stills to tell an embarrassing story about sneaking out the back when the police broke up one of the Laurel Canyon house party/jam sessions where the performers tried out their music, inspired each other’s work and got high. ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/05/31/arts/30echopix/merlin_155326896_12b98a42-e366-4a79-8536-9615c5b02930-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 338, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2019/05/31/arts/30echopix/merlin_155326896_12b98a42-e366-4a79-8536-9615c5b02930-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 338}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/05/31/arts/30echopix/merlin_155326896_12b98a42-e366-4a79-8536-9615c5b02930-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 576, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/05/31/arts/30echopix/merlin_155326896_12b98a42-e366-4a79-8536-9615c5b02930-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1080, 'width': 1920, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/05/31/arts/30echopix/merlin_155326896_12b98a42-e366-4a79-8536-9615c5b02930-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2019/05/31/arts/30echopix/merlin_155326896_12b98a42-e366-4a79-8536-9615c5b02930-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/05/31/arts/30echopix/merlin_155326896_12b98a42-e366-4a79-8536-9615c5b02930-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': '‘Echo in the Canyon’ Review: Capturing a California Musical Moment', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Echo in the Canyon', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'Echo In the Canyon (Movie)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Documentary Films and Programs', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'SLATER, ANDREW', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2019-05-30T11:00:06+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Weekend', 'section_name': 'Movies', 'byline': {'original': 'By Helen T. Verongos', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Helen', 'middlename': 'T.', 'lastname': 'Verongos', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/111e81c8-3f00-5461-8595-b360c99f6ddd', 'word_count': 304, 'uri': 'nyt://article/111e81c8-3f00-5461-8595-b360c99f6ddd'}, {'abstract': 'A.B. Shawky’s empathetic feature film follows a former leper through Egypt as he searches for the family who abandoned him.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2019/05/30/movies/yomeddine-review.html', 'snippet': 'A.B. Shawky’s empathetic feature film follows a former leper through Egypt as he searches for the family who abandoned him.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The star and hero of the warm drama “Yomeddine,” Beshay, is a survivor of leprosy, who has lived in a leper colony in northern Egypt for most of his life. In the seclusion of the colony, he is married and makes his living picking up and selling trash from a local landfill. As played by the magnetic Rady Gamal, a cafeteria worker who was himself cured of leprosy, Beshay’s face and hands bear the scars of illness, but his pride remains intact.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '7', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/05/31/arts/30yomeddine2/merlin_155261727_f99475d5-a2f0-43ac-a7b5-a5ed93a81fd4-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 338, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2019/05/31/arts/30yomeddine2/merlin_155261727_f99475d5-a2f0-43ac-a7b5-a5ed93a81fd4-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 338}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/05/31/arts/30yomeddine2/merlin_155261727_f99475d5-a2f0-43ac-a7b5-a5ed93a81fd4-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 576, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/05/31/arts/30yomeddine2/merlin_155261727_f99475d5-a2f0-43ac-a7b5-a5ed93a81fd4-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1152, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/05/31/arts/30yomeddine2/30yomeddine2-thumbSta