 playing third-round matches at Roland Garros.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The only two lines from the 1999 French Open men’s singles draw that appeared again for this year’s tournament are: R. Federer (SUI) and C. Ruud (NOR). Roger Federer provides continuity, but the other player is a successor: Casper Ruud, who was five months old when his father, Christian, competed at Roland Garros two decades ago. Casper, now 20, will face Federer, 37, in the second match on Suzanne Lenglen Court. Though many players of Ruud’s generation have idolized Federer, Ruud is more of a Nadal guy, basing himself out of the Rafael Nadal Academy in Majorca.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/06/30/sports/30tenniswatch1/30tenniswatch1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 379, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2019/06/30/sports/30tenniswatch1/30tenniswatch1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 379}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/06/30/sports/30tenniswatch1/30tenniswatch1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 647, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/06/30/sports/30tenniswatch1/30tenniswatch1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1294, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/06/30/sports/30tenniswatch1/30tenniswatch1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2019/06/30/sports/30tenniswatch1/30tenniswatch1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 't