e Weeknight Dishes, recipes for busy people who still want something good to eat. I have a tendency to go wild with herbs when I’m cooking, tossing them with abandon into salads and over vegetables, pasta and meat. My latest love is dill, fresh and feathery, thanks to the writer Naz Deravian and her Persian cookbook, “Bottom of the Pot.” I cooked a lot from it when I judged a round of the Piglet tournament of cookbooks on Food52 in March, and in that time my fridge became a leafy, branchy wonderland of herbs, which figure prominently in Persian cooking. (You can read our own Samin Nosrat on this very subject!)', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/05/22/dining/nd-sheveed-polo/merlin_154348143_542cc6cf-4c27-4692-bcea-6be80dc7e7ef-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2019/05/22/dining/nd-sheveed-polo/merlin_154348143_542cc6cf-4c27-4692-bcea-6be80dc7e7ef-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/05/22/dining/nd-sheveed-polo/merlin_154348143_542cc6cf-4c27-4692-bcea-6be80dc7e7ef-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/05/22/dining/nd-sheveed-polo/merlin_154348143_542cc6cf-4c27-4692-bcea-6be80dc7e7ef-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/05/22/dining/nd-sheveed-polo/nd-sheveed-polo-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'imag